00:49:25.671 --> 00:49:26.504
brushed himself,

1584
00:49:26.504 --> 00:49:27.924
and then carried on running

1585
00:49:27.924 --> 00:49:29.499
and the doors of the tube shut.

1586
00:49:29.499 --> 00:49:30.332
And it went.

1587
00:49:30.332 --> 00:49:32.495
And when I finally arrive at the platform

1588
00:49:32.495 --> 00:49:33.328
and I look up,

1589
00:49:33.328 --> 00:49:35.800
the next one's in two minutes, you know,

1590
00:49:35.800 --> 00:49:38.681
because the tube trains are every two minutes, right?

1591
00:49:38.681 --> 00:49:39.514
Right.

1592
00:49:39.514 --> 00:49:40.347
It's two minutes to the next one, right?

1593
00:49:40.347 --> 00:49:42.716
So the induced state of panic

1594
00:49:42.716 --> 00:49:44.024
for no real benefit,

1595
00:49:44.024 --> 00:49:45.764
like there's no payoff

1596
00:49:45.764 --> 00:49:50.099
for inducing that like state of fear and anxiety.

1597
00:49:50.099 --> 00:49:51.657
Yeah and it starts like it...

1598
00:49:51.657 --> 00:49:52.968
I mean there's stages to it.

1599
00:49:52.968 --> 00:49:53.806
It's accumulative.

1600
00:49:53.806 --> 00:49:55.563
And unless we find practices

1601
00:49:55.563 --> 00:49:58.054
that enable us to step outside of it,

1602
00:49:58.054 --> 00:50:00.502
this is by experiences or you could go on retreats, right?

1603
00:50:00.502 --> 00:50:01.335
Or workshops-

1604
00:50:01.335 --> 00:50:03.274
they enable us to get tools

1605
00:50:03.274 --> 00:50:05.486
that we can then bring into those everyday environments,

1606
00:50:05.486 --> 00:50:06.319
right?

1607
00:50:06.319 --> 00:50:09.276
That can change our... maybe even our internal beliefs,

1608
00:50:09.276 --> 00:50:11.682
but certainly allow us to step outside

1609
00:50:11.682 --> 00:50:14.287
those everyday behaviors that perhaps aren't serving us.

1610
00:50:14.287 --> 00:50:15.120
Right?

1611
00:50:15.120 --> 00:50:16.792
And then to make real change, I can come back,

1612
00:50:16.792 --> 00:50:18.465
"oh, suddenly... oh, how about this?"

1613
00:50:18.465 --> 00:50:20.488
In the lyrics of my friend Nick Mulvey,

1614
00:50:20.488 --> 00:50:22.590
"Happy is the man that breathes in the morning,"

1615
00:50:22.590 --> 00:50:23.423
right?

1616
00:50:23.423 --> 00:50:25.850
So it could be, right, I just sit

1617
00:50:25.850 --> 00:50:27.156
and I just do some breath work.

1618
00:50:27.156 --> 00:50:29.549
In bed even, just opened my eyes instead of going,

1619
00:50:29.549 --> 00:50:31.364
"right, there's my phone" and checking in,

1620
00:50:31.364 --> 00:50:32.395
just check in with yourself.

1621
00:50:32.395 --> 00:50:34.494
Just breathe for a moment. Downregulation.

1622
00:50:34.494 --> 00:50:38.118
Start calm, you know? And then try and remain calm.

1623
00:50:38.118 --> 00:50:39.279
And I'd prefer even

1624
00:50:39.279 --> 00:50:42.778
to rock up two minutes late for something calm

1625
00:50:42.778 --> 00:50:44.604
than I would to be an upregulated mess,

1626
00:50:44.604 --> 00:50:46.851
because it's about then who's receiving me-

1627
00:50:46.851 --> 00:50:47.684
Right.

1628
00:50:47.684 --> 00:50:48.676
...and what am I bringing into that environment?

1629
00:50:48.676 --> 00:50:49.509
Yeah, what energy are you-

1630
00:50:49.509 --> 00:50:50.342
You know?

1631
00:50:50.342 --> 00:50:51.590
And then everyone else goes all upregulated.

1632
00:50:51.590 --> 00:50:52.423
Right.

1633
00:50:52.423 --> 00:50:53.256
Imagine, it'd like-

1634
00:50:53.256 --> 00:50:54.719
You're not getting a good result out of that.

1635
00:50:54.719 --> 00:50:55.552
No.

1636
00:50:55.552 --> 00:50:56.979
It's like turning up for a meeting

1637
00:50:56.979 --> 00:50:58.172
or imagine an interview

1638
00:50:58.172 --> 00:50:59.143
or whatever it is

1639
00:50:59.143 --> 00:51:00.253
and you're in that state.

1640
00:51:00.253 --> 00:51:02.427
And I go for a lot of these practices with our kids

1641
00:51:02.427 --> 00:51:05.427
