00:51:15.085 --> 00:51:17.533
Imagine mock exams, Rich, were about,

1649
00:51:17.533 --> 00:51:19.307
oh, you go through these practices

1650
00:51:19.307 --> 00:51:20.914
as well as doing the exam

1651
00:51:20.914 --> 00:51:23.093
so that you can remain calm in that situation.

1652
00:51:23.093 --> 00:51:23.939
Because, you know what?

1653
00:51:23.939 --> 00:51:24.794
This exam's gonna...

1654
00:51:24.794 --> 00:51:26.525
this might be how the rest of your life plays out

1655
00:51:26.525 --> 00:51:27.829
in this moment, right?

1656
00:51:27.829 --> 00:51:28.881
And for some it is,

1657
00:51:28.881 --> 00:51:31.321
there's so much involved in their education

1658
00:51:31.321 --> 00:51:32.580
that that's their careers and everything

1659
00:51:32.580 --> 00:51:34.188
for the rest of their lives,

1660
00:51:34.188 --> 00:51:35.209
but not being taught well,

1661
00:51:35.209 --> 00:51:37.441
these are practices that will enable you

1662
00:51:37.441 --> 00:51:38.988
to think smarter in that environment, you know?

1663
00:51:38.988 --> 00:51:39.821
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

1664
00:51:39.821 --> 00:51:42.304
And behave differently within it, you know?

1665
00:51:42.304 --> 00:51:44.224
So what would be one of those practices?

1666
00:51:44.224 --> 00:51:46.109
I mean, you took us through the simplest

1667
00:51:46.109 --> 00:51:47.283
of breath exercises,

1668
00:51:47.283 --> 00:51:49.121
but I know you do a lot of stuff

1669
00:51:49.121 --> 00:51:51.646
with like alternating nasal breaths.

1670
00:51:51.646 --> 00:51:55.865
Like what would be one tool that you could give to people?

1671
00:51:55.865 --> 00:51:59.306
I would work with those extended exhales, really.

1672
00:51:59.306 --> 00:52:01.786
Like if you put your finger on your pulse when you inhale,

1673
00:52:01.786 --> 00:52:04.075
you'll notice your pulse picks up

1674
00:52:04.075 --> 00:52:06.244
and then as you exhale, you get a lowering of your pulse.

1675
00:52:06.244 --> 00:52:07.818
So it's tuning to that lowering of the pulse.

1676
00:52:07.818 --> 00:52:09.026
So even if you had someone that...

1677
00:52:09.026 --> 00:52:10.442
you know, blood pressure, right?

1678
00:52:10.442 --> 00:52:12.541
"Oh, I'm gonna go and have my blood pressure read."

1679
00:52:12.541 --> 00:52:13.374
Go to the doctor's,

1680
00:52:13.374 --> 00:52:14.733
blood pressure goes up for most people

1681
00:52:14.733 --> 00:52:15.945
when they enter the doctor's, right?

1682
00:52:15.945 --> 00:52:17.882
But if you had started extending your exhales,

1683
00:52:17.882 --> 00:52:18.715
you'd have a different outcome.

1684
00:52:18.715 --> 00:52:19.972
So think of it like that.

1685
00:52:19.972 --> 00:52:21.277
I start to extend exhales.

1686
00:52:21.277 --> 00:52:23.577
It's... whenever I've been on radio

1687
00:52:23.577 --> 00:52:26.157
or it's been T.V. which was new for me.

1688
00:52:26.157 --> 00:52:28.775
I used to sit and just put a breathing app on.

1689
00:52:28.775 --> 00:52:30.780
I put this on now this is by Eddie Stern.

1690
00:52:30.780 --> 00:52:32.939
Eddie Stern's like a Ashtanga teacher

1691
00:52:32.939 --> 00:52:34.842
that put this free app out into the world.

1692
00:52:34.842 --> 00:52:36.316
It's brilliant; it's genius.

1693
00:52:36.316 --> 00:52:38.416
And it just has a sliding scale of...

1694
00:52:38.416 --> 00:52:39.790
and you can set ratios on there.

1695
00:52:39.790 --> 00:52:42.049
So this is like a four...

1696
00:52:42.049 --> 00:52:46.302
(two low-pitched tones play)

1697
00:52:46.302 --> 00:52:48.209
four seconds in, six seconds out.

1698
00:52:48.209 --> 00:52:49.042
Mmm.

1699
00:52:49.042 --> 00:52:50.830
And it just gives you that tone.

1700
00:52:50.830 --> 00:52:52.152
It has a circle on that inflates

1701
00:52:52.152 --> 00:52:53.311
