1843
00:57:02.380 --> 00:57:04.551
And so it's as if you're foraging off the ground like that,

1844
00:57:04.551 --> 00:57:05.586
but now you are hoovering instead

1845
00:57:05.586 --> 00:57:07.299
'cause we no longer forage off the ground.

1846
00:57:07.299 --> 00:57:09.156
And then others might be like crawling, right?

1847
00:57:09.156 --> 00:57:10.891
Now you have to think of weird and wonderful ways

1848
00:57:10.891 --> 00:57:12.152
to crawl around your apartment,

1849
00:57:12.152 --> 00:57:15.240
because, again, it's hugely nourishing, right?

1850
00:57:15.240 --> 00:57:16.073
Mm-hmm.

1851
00:57:16.073 --> 00:57:17.116
And it's stuff that we've lost

1852
00:57:17.116 --> 00:57:18.096
within this landscape.

1853
00:57:18.096 --> 00:57:19.795
And the thing about this landscape, unfortunately, again,

1854
00:57:19.795 --> 00:57:22.160
on that term of neuroplasticity,

1855
00:57:22.160 --> 00:57:24.491
we are literally just moving from one linear box

1856
00:57:24.491 --> 00:57:27.486
to another linear box on another linear street, right?

1857
00:57:27.486 --> 00:57:29.683
With headphones in or heads down in phones.

1858
00:57:29.683 --> 00:57:32.355
So it's how can we nourish that

1859
00:57:32.355 --> 00:57:34.253
within those urban environments?

1860
00:57:34.253 --> 00:57:37.186
So again, it's, you know, it's not demonizing the city,

1861
00:57:37.186 --> 00:57:38.763
but it's finding ways of living within it

1862
00:57:38.763 --> 00:57:41.558
that are enhancing, you know?

1863
00:57:41.558 --> 00:57:42.391
Right.

1864
00:57:42.391 --> 00:57:44.790
And it does require you to kind of

1865
00:57:44.790 --> 00:57:46.691
set aside your ego a little bit,

1866
00:57:46.691 --> 00:57:47.524
I mean,

1867
00:57:47.524 --> 00:57:48.955
you have all these videos of you

1868
00:57:48.955 --> 00:57:50.118
like crawling around on the ground with your kids

1869
00:57:50.118 --> 00:57:52.217
and like waving your arms, flapping your arms around

1870
00:57:52.217 --> 00:57:53.080
and stuff like that.

1871
00:57:53.080 --> 00:57:55.814
Like, there's a little bit of shared DNA

1872
00:57:55.814 --> 00:57:57.978
with Ito Portal and the work that he does,

1873
00:57:57.978 --> 00:57:59.861
like bringing play into all of this.

1874
00:57:59.861 --> 00:58:00.694
Yeah.

1875
00:58:00.694 --> 00:58:02.145
Making it joyous and fun

1876
00:58:02.145 --> 00:58:05.150
and not being so self-conscious like,

1877
00:58:05.150 --> 00:58:05.983
you know,

1878
00:58:05.983 --> 00:58:07.880
we're not gonna be able to go down on Portobello road

1879
00:58:07.880 --> 00:58:08.713
and crawl around,

1880
00:58:08.713 --> 00:58:10.784
you know, like, we might get arrested.

1881
00:58:10.784 --> 00:58:11.617
I don't know.

1882
00:58:11.617 --> 00:58:12.843
You probably do this or have done it.

1883
00:58:12.843 --> 00:58:13.676
I don't...

1884
00:58:13.676 --> 00:58:14.509
(Rich laughs)

1885
00:58:14.509 --> 00:58:15.342
...you know.

1886
00:58:15.342 --> 00:58:16.811
But I, you know, it's like people are gonna clam up.

1887
00:58:16.811 --> 00:58:17.742
Like-

1888
00:58:17.742 --> 00:58:18.622
Yeah.

1889
00:58:18.622 --> 00:58:19.527
" I can't be that way in the world."

1890
00:58:19.527 --> 00:58:20.391
Right?

1891
00:58:20.391 --> 00:58:21.438
Yeah.

1892
00:58:21.438 --> 00:58:23.187
Like, but how can we let go a little bit of that?

1893
00:58:23.187 --> 00:58:24.944
I mean, you've got a quote something about like,

1894
00:58:24.944 --> 00:58:29.267
"we have to become less ego-conscious and more eco-conscious

1895
00:58:29.267 --> 00:58:32.317
and 'eco' being broadly defined as, you know,

1896
00:58:32.317 --> 00:58:35.503
our physical vessels but also our environment

1897
00:58:35.503 --> 00:58:37.412
in which we, you know, share.

1898
00:58:37.412 --> 00:58:38.245
Yeah.

1899
00:58:38.245 --> 00:58:40.918
So, it's disconnecting from the egosystem

1900
00:58:40.918 --> 00:58:42.706
and reconnecting to our ecosystem.

1901
00:58:42.706 --> 00:58:43.539
Mmm.

1902
00:58:43.539 --> 00:58:44.610
And there's practices in there

1903
00:58:44.610 --> 00:58:45.443
that I call re-childing, right?

1904
00:58:45.443 --> 00:58:48.891
So it's about taking people through a process

1905
00:58:48.891 --> 00:58:52.884
so that they can remove all that armor and awkwardness

1906
00:58:52.884 --> 00:58:53.717
that comes.

1907
00:58:53.717 --> 00:58:55.895
You know, it's like when did adulthood,

1908
00:58:55.895 --> 00:58:56.879
when did it become so serious?

1909
00:58:56.879 --> 00:58:57.712
Right?

1910
00:58:57.712 --> 00:59:00.130
When was that? What was the point?

1911
00:59:00.130 --> 00:59:03.483
And I often talk about schooling 'cause we un-school

1912
00:59:03.483 --> 00:59:05.238
and it's not, again, to demonize schooling,

1913
00:59:05.238 --> 00:59:06.181
but it's to say, well,

1914
00:59:06.181 --> 00:59:08.850
"what happens within that schooling environment?"

1915
00:59:08.850 --> 00:59:09.683
Right?

1916
00:59:09.683 --> 00:59:11.768
Whereas we are very playful.

1917
00:59:11.768 --> 00:59:13.944
If I look at my youngest,

1918
00:59:13.944 --> 00:59:16.904
he's like, just play the whole time.

1919
00:59:16.904 --> 00:59:17.817
Right?

1920
00:59:17.817 --> 00:59:19.479
He's even playing with his emotions

1921
00:59:19.479 --> 00:59:20.651
when he let's rip and just,

1922
00:59:20.651 --> 00:59:23.081
you know, starts tearing the house down

1923
00:59:23.081 --> 00:59:24.116
or whatever he's doing.

1924
00:59:24.116 --> 00:59:26.703
He's still playing; he's playing with emotions.

1925
00:59:26.703 --> 00:59:28.974
And then Tallulah is like, she's our Boudica.

1926
00:59:28.974 --> 00:59:31.072
She's like really wild and roaring

1927
00:59:31.072 --> 00:59:31.905
and you know,

1928
00:59:31.905 --> 00:59:32.744
she's full of energy.

1929
00:59:32.744 --> 00:59:34.557
But they're so playful,

1930
00:59:34.557 --> 00:59:37.491
and so that's up until... Tallulah's now six.

1931
00:59:37.491 --> 00:59:39.591
So she would be ready for school, right?

1932
00:59:39.591 --> 00:59:40.424
Five or six.

1933
00:59:40.424 --> 00:59:42.220
And then you enter that environment

1934
00:59:42.220 --> 00:59:43.599
and then that play

1935
00:59:43.599 --> 00:59:45.810
that you're allowed to play with all your emotions

1936
00:59:45.810 --> 00:59:47.115
and your expressions

1937
00:59:47.115 --> 00:59:48.824
is suddenly in a container, right?

1938
00:59:48.824 --> 00:59:49.657
In a linear room-

1939
00:59:49.657 --> 00:59:50.490
Mm-hmm.

1940
00:59:50.490 --> 00:59:51.323
...all of a sudden.

1941
00:59:51.323 --> 00:59:52.910
In a chair with a hierarchal system

1942
00:59:52.910 --> 00:59:55.050
and suddenly you're no longer allowed to speak

1943
00:59:55.050 --> 00:59:57.253
when you would normally just let rip

1944
00:59:57.253 --> 00:59:58.329
and just let stuff go.

1945
00:59:58.329 --> 01:00:00.069
So we all then get a bit locked up even

1946
01:00:00.069 --> 01:00:01.972
in our throat chakras if you think about that

1947
01:00:01.972 --> 01:00:03.545
from a very early age, right?

1948
01:00:03.545 --> 01:00:05.582
So that's expression that goes,

1949
01:00:05.582 --> 01:00:08.322
and then we are allowed out to play in an environment

1950
01:00:08.322 --> 01:00:10.166
that is adult-led in a way, right?

1951
01:00:10.166 --> 01:00:11.026
It's painted lines-

1952
01:00:11.026 --> 01:00:11.859
Mm-hmm.

1953
01:00:11.859 --> 01:00:12.692
...and stuff that we think

1954
01:00:12.692 --> 01:00:13.525
they would want to play around on.

1955
01:00:13.525 --> 01:00:14.601
Right, there's very specific parameters

1956
01:00:14.601 --> 01:00:16.718
of what that play can and can't be.

1957
01:00:16.718 --> 01:00:18.638
Yeah. And within health and safety, right?

1958
01:00:18.638 --> 01:00:20.428
So it's not... this isn't...

1959
01:00:20.428 --> 01:00:21.261
again,

1960
01:00:21.261 --> 01:00:22.094
it's not the schooling,

1961
01:00:22.094 --> 01:00:25.302
it's the systems that we've created over time, right?

1962
01:00:25.302 --> 01:00:26.941
And then within that,

1963
01:00:26.941 --> 01:00:29.429
you'll then return back to the classroom environment

1964
01:00:29.429 --> 01:00:31.843
and then over time that play experience

1965
01:00:31.843 --> 01:00:33.271
becomes lunch break, right?

1966
01:00:33.271 --> 01:00:36.101
And then you have P.E. and P.E. is then very specialized,

1967
01:00:36.101 --> 01:00:36.934
less generalist,

1968
01:00:36.934 --> 01:00:41.107
very... there is play within it, but it's specialist play.

1969
01:00:41.107 --> 01:00:42.806
So it becomes a sport, right?

1970
01:00:42.806 --> 01:00:46.780
And it's repetition and repetition of movement in a way.

1971
01:00:46.780 --> 01:00:49.031
So my practice has been...

1972
01:00:49.031 --> 01:00:51.034
we have these workshops now

1973
01:00:51.034 --> 01:00:53.230
called the "100 Human Experience,"

1974
01:00:53.230 --> 01:00:56.032
and it starts with an opening circle, usually around a fire,

1975
01:00:56.032 --> 01:00:57.205
and then we set intentions

1976
01:00:57.205 --> 01:00:59.864
and we have people kind of intro'd within it

1977
01:00:59.864 --> 01:01:01.009
and then I open up play.

1978
01:01:01.009 --> 01:01:02.912
So it's, now the circle opens up,

1979
01:01:02.912 --> 01:01:05.123
and I have people just meandering around in a circle

1980
01:01:05.123 --> 01:01:05.956
and they walk around,

1981
01:01:05.956 --> 01:01:06.789
they brush shoulders,

1982
01:01:06.789 --> 01:01:07.630
and they make eye contact.

1983
01:01:07.630 --> 01:01:10.269
Now, they bump shoulders and bump bums together

1984
01:01:10.269 --> 01:01:11.670
and all of a sudden laughter comes immediately.

1985
01:01:11.670 --> 01:01:12.503
It's done.

1986
01:01:12.503 --> 01:01:13.336
Right?

1987
01:01:13.336 --> 01:01:14.169
Within five minutes,

1988
01:01:14.169 --> 01:01:16.181
complete strangers suddenly just giggling away

1989
01:01:16.181 --> 01:01:17.796
and then it continues, right, now you stop

1990
01:01:17.796 --> 01:01:19.232
and you hold their shoulders, you look at them in the eyes,

1991
01:01:19.232 --> 01:01:20.448
and then you carry on walking.

1992
01:01:20.448 --> 01:01:21.563
And then eventually it's like, all right,

1993
01:01:21.563 --> 01:01:22.858
you stop, make eye contact,

1994
01:01:22.858 --> 01:01:23.797
really strong eye contact,

1995
01:01:23.797 --> 01:01:24.664
then walk off again.

1996
01:01:24.664 --> 01:01:26.164
Because if you'll notice here,

1997
01:01:26.164 --> 01:01:28.802
very little eye contact will occur in where we are right now

1998
01:01:28.802 --> 01:01:29.635
in London.

1999
01:01:29.635 --> 01:01:30.468
You know?

2000
01:01:30.468 --> 01:01:31.874
And then eventually those layers,

2001
01:01:31.874 --> 01:01:32.707
those facades,

2002
01:01:32.707 --> 01:01:35.840
that armor is broken down with 100 complete strangers.

2003
01:01:35.840 --> 01:01:37.440
Suddenly start working as one;

2004
01:01:37.440 --> 01:01:39.771
that collective bonding starts to occur.

2005
01:01:39.771 --> 01:01:41.126
And then I have them holding each other's shoulders

2006
01:01:41.126 --> 01:01:43.213
and then yelling into each other's eyes, "you are loved."

2007
01:01:43.213 --> 01:01:44.046
Right?

2008
01:01:44.046 --> 01:01:44.883
And all of a sudden

2009
01:01:44.883 --> 01:01:46.084
you can see people just cracking at that moment.

2010
01:01:46.084 --> 01:01:46.917
Right?

2011
01:01:46.917 --> 01:01:48.005
It's very emotional, even,

2012
01:01:48.005 --> 01:01:49.310
just to have someone look at you in the eyes

2013
01:01:49.310 --> 01:01:50.315
and say "you are loved!"

2014
01:01:50.315 --> 01:01:52.110
And especially after you've dealt with

2015
01:01:52.110 --> 01:01:53.749
getting the armor away that's broken through

2016
01:01:53.749 --> 01:01:55.410
that allows that emotion.

2017
01:01:55.410 --> 01:01:56.580
And then it continues

2018
01:01:56.580 --> 01:01:59.160
and it turns into this very playful...

2019
01:01:59.160 --> 01:02:01.974
there's so much humor and belly laughter

2020
01:02:01.974 --> 01:02:03.899
that is in that moment.

2021
01:02:03.899 --> 01:02:05.820
And when we return back to the circle

2022
01:02:05.820 --> 01:02:08.861
before going into the next practice which is usually breath,

2023
01:02:08.861 --> 01:02:10.511
the sharing is always, you know-

2024
01:02:10.511 --> 01:02:11.344
Sure.

2025
01:02:11.344 --> 01:02:13.517
You know, "oh my God, it's as if

2026
01:02:13.517 --> 01:02:15.100
I've just reentered back there

2027
01:02:15.100 --> 01:02:16.874
and I can't believe that I gave all that away."

2028
01:02:16.874 --> 01:02:17.707
Mm-hmm.

2029
01:02:17.707 --> 01:02:18.685
You know?

2030
01:02:18.685 --> 01:02:22.252
And that's re-childing just as that's re-wilding,

2031
01:02:22.252 --> 01:02:23.800
but it's re-childing for me.

2032
01:02:23.800 --> 01:02:26.787
And you know, it's such a powerful, powerful practice

2033
01:02:26.787 --> 01:02:30.834
almost beyond what the breath work and the ice bath is

2034
01:02:30.834 --> 01:02:33.695
because you're stripping away many, many layers there.

2035
01:02:33.695 --> 01:02:34.528
Mm-hmm.

2036
01:02:34.528 --> 01:02:36.704
And going back into a playful state of mind

2037
01:02:36.704 --> 01:02:38.523
It's like play isn't just play,

2038
01:02:38.523 --> 01:02:42.148
it's a state of mind which then opens up new worlds.

2039
01:02:42.148 --> 01:02:43.294
And we have people that...

2040
01:02:43.294 --> 01:02:45.416
well we've all been stuck at some point, right?

2041
01:02:45.416 --> 01:02:48.583
And we get stuck and we almost get stuck in a character

2042
01:02:48.583 --> 01:02:51.518
and we can get stuck in a character of depression.

2043
01:02:51.518 --> 01:02:52.790
I'm holding men's circles,

2044
01:02:52.790 --> 01:02:54.574
and the amount of guys that come on those circles

2045
01:02:54.574 --> 01:02:56.670
who are locked in with depression, right?

2046
01:02:56.670 --> 01:02:58.751
And we go through the same practice,

2047
01:02:58.751 --> 01:03:00.136
like really playful stuff,

2048
01:03:00.136 --> 01:03:03.783
and it's a way all of a sudden of reconnecting

2049
01:03:03.783 --> 01:03:05.975
with your imagination brain, let's say.

2050
01:03:05.975 --> 01:03:06.808
Right?

2051
01:03:06.808 --> 01:03:08.474
And you can imagine yourself

2052
01:03:08.474 --> 01:03:10.570
as a different being altogether.

2053
01:03:10.570 --> 01:03:11.571
You can imagine yourself

2054
01:03:11.571 --> 01:03:13.719
in a completely different position in life.

2055
01:03:13.719 --> 01:03:14.634
You can imagine yourself

2056
01:03:14.634 --> 01:03:16.256
as someone completely different

2057
01:03:16.256 --> 01:03:18.495
to the person that's stuck right now.

2058
01:03:18.495 --> 01:03:21.026
And they reawaken from that through acts of play.

2059
01:03:21.026 --> 01:03:22.522
There's trauma work in play.

2060
01:03:22.522 --> 01:03:25.155
It's fascinating when you go into it like

2061
01:03:25.155 --> 01:03:28.742
as a modality for dealing with mental health issues, even,

2062
01:03:28.742 --> 01:03:29.575
Right?

2063
01:03:29.575 --> 01:03:30.408
Hmmm.

2064
01:03:30.408 --> 01:03:31.241
And then we have to say,

2065
01:03:31.241 --> 01:03:32.074
"well, where does that stuff enter?

2066
01:03:32.074 --> 01:03:33.101
Oh, well, is it perhaps

2067
01:03:33.101 --> 01:03:34.834
when I had my playful state of mind removed?

2068
01:03:34.834 --> 01:03:36.103
Could it be that?

2069
01:03:36.103 --> 01:03:37.622
That I no longer can imagine myself

2070
01:03:37.622 --> 01:03:38.676
in these different worlds?"

2071
01:03:38.676 --> 01:03:41.351
And well I think we talked about this on the last podcast;

2072
01:03:41.351 --> 01:03:42.901
there's that...

2073
01:03:42.901 --> 01:03:44.204
there's Peter Gray

2074
01:03:44.204 --> 01:03:45.687
who wrote this book called "Free to Learn."

2075
01:03:45.687 --> 01:03:46.520
Right?

2076
01:03:46.520 --> 01:03:48.148
So I'm gonna mention it again

2077
01:03:48.148 --> 01:03:49.922
'cause I think it's really valuable,

2078
01:03:49.922 --> 01:03:52.021
as he asked 10 leading anthropologists

2079
01:03:52.021 --> 01:03:54.343
what play looks like in nature.

2080
01:03:54.343 --> 01:03:55.871
And they look at three independent tribes,

2081
01:03:55.871 --> 01:03:58.002
different geographic locations.

2082
01:03:58.002 --> 01:04:00.101
And first, the first thing they come back with,

2083
01:04:00.101 --> 01:04:01.138
all of them,

2084
01:04:01.138 --> 01:04:03.241
it's like they're the most well-adjusted, well-rounded

2085
01:04:03.241 --> 01:04:04.778
individuals they've ever met, right-

2086
01:04:04.778 --> 01:04:05.611
Mm-hmm.

2087
01:04:05.611 --> 01:04:06.444
...are the children.

2088
01:04:06.444 --> 01:04:07.277
Mm-hmm.

2089
01:04:07.277 --> 01:04:08.110
And what does it look like?

2090
01:04:08.110 --> 01:04:08.943
And they said,

2091
01:04:08.943 --> 01:04:09.937
"well, from infancy through to teenage years,

2092
01:04:09.937 --> 01:04:12.036
all the kids do is play."

2093
01:04:12.036 --> 01:04:15.868
And they play at being everything within the environment

2094
01:04:15.868 --> 01:04:18.100
so they play at the adults.

2095
01:04:18.100 --> 01:04:20.011
So imagine, through that experience,

2096
01:04:20.011 --> 01:04:21.460
they have birth, they have death,

2097
01:04:21.460 --> 01:04:24.375
they have all these different rites of passage that occur,

2098
01:04:24.375 --> 01:04:25.856
but also they learn to track animals.

2099
01:04:25.856 --> 01:04:27.167
They learn that stuff

2100
01:04:27.167 --> 01:04:28.656
that I've taught people blindfolded to go into.

2101
01:04:28.656 --> 01:04:29.510
They learn foraging skills,

2102
01:04:29.510 --> 01:04:30.857
they can build shelters,

2103
01:04:30.857 --> 01:04:31.806
they can track.

2104
01:04:31.806 --> 01:04:35.285
So suddenly they enter adulthood.

2105
01:04:35.285 --> 01:04:36.583
Is adulthood any different then?

2106
01:04:36.583 --> 01:04:38.804
Isn't it not just the playful state of mind

2107
01:04:38.804 --> 01:04:39.724
that they're achieving,

2108
01:04:39.724 --> 01:04:40.970
they're managing to walk around with.

2109
01:04:40.970 --> 01:04:42.626
It then brings Bruce Parry's work in

2110
01:04:42.626 --> 01:04:45.240
where they're in this permanent state of meditation

2111
01:04:45.240 --> 01:04:46.666
that you and I can only achieve.

2112
01:04:46.666 --> 01:04:47.827
Is that possible for us then,

2113
01:04:47.827 --> 01:04:48.660
you know,

2114
01:04:48.660 --> 01:04:50.762
if you think about, if you've really unpacked it that way?

2115
01:04:50.762 --> 01:04:53.689
So there's so much to that playful state of mind

2116
01:04:53.689 --> 01:04:55.268
that we could open up and unpack.

2117
01:04:55.268 --> 01:04:56.101
Yeah.

2118
01:04:56.101 --> 01:05:00.219
The level of layers, the extent to which we build these,

2119
01:05:00.219 --> 01:05:02.960
you know, castles around our identities

2120
01:05:02.960 --> 01:05:07.227
and our personas and the adherence to social constructs

2121
01:05:07.227 --> 01:05:08.157
and rules,

2122
01:05:08.157 --> 01:05:11.120
all of that calcifies our ability

2123
01:05:11.120 --> 01:05:12.953
to just be who we are.

2124
01:05:14.091 --> 01:05:17.335
And 'play,' by its own definition,

2125
01:05:17.335 --> 01:05:18.835
requires a sort of

2126
01:05:20.074 --> 01:05:23.829
transcendency of the logical, rational-

2127
01:05:23.829 --> 01:05:24.662
Hmmm.

2128
01:05:24.662 --> 01:05:27.997
...you know, like looping mind, right?

2129
01:05:27.997 --> 01:05:29.814
It is a flow state of sorts

2130
01:05:29.814 --> 01:05:31.176
in the sense that

2131
01:05:31.176 --> 01:05:32.248
when you're playing,

2132
01:05:32.248 --> 01:05:34.635
you're not really thinking about what you're doing,

2133
01:05:34.635 --> 01:05:35.975
you're being, right?

2134
01:05:35.975 --> 01:05:38.615
And when you're being, there isn't room

2135
01:05:38.615 --> 01:05:41.684
for all of those narratives to get in the way.

2136
01:05:41.684 --> 01:05:42.517
Right?

2137
01:05:42.517 --> 01:05:45.070
But the more we erect these walls around ourselves,

2138
01:05:45.070 --> 01:05:48.735
the more difficult it is to connect with that

2139
01:05:48.735 --> 01:05:50.352
primal state of play

2140
01:05:50.352 --> 01:05:54.104
because the ego intercedes and tells us like,

2141
01:05:54.104 --> 01:05:56.212
"you'll look like an idiot if you do that."

2142
01:05:56.212 --> 01:05:57.045
Hmm.

2143
01:05:57.045 --> 01:05:57.878
Or, you know,

2144
01:05:57.878 --> 01:05:59.189
"what is somebody gonna say

2145
01:05:59.189 --> 01:06:00.837
if you behave in this certain way?"

2146
01:06:00.837 --> 01:06:04.307
And all of these things create a prison of our own making-

2147
01:06:04.307 --> 01:06:05.140
Yeah.

2148
01:06:05.140 --> 01:06:06.253
... that is driving...

2149
01:06:06.253 --> 01:06:09.047
you know it's obviously more complicated than that,

2150
01:06:09.047 --> 01:06:11.952
but you know, has to be on some level at the root

2151
01:06:11.952 --> 01:06:14.815
of some of these, you know, depressive tendencies

2152
01:06:14.815 --> 01:06:16.366
that we're seeing on the rise.

2153
01:06:16.366 --> 01:06:18.835
Yeah, I, again, I think it goes back to

2154
01:06:18.835 --> 01:06:21.233
imagining yourself in other realms, even.

2155
01:06:21.233 --> 01:06:22.066
You know?

2156
01:06:22.066 --> 01:06:24.721
And those kids in nature again,

2157
01:06:24.721 --> 01:06:27.621
they're learning everything about their environment.

2158
01:06:27.621 --> 01:06:29.569
I mean that's one consciousness, is it not?

2159
01:06:29.569 --> 01:06:30.967
That's understanding real biodiversity,

2160
01:06:30.967 --> 01:06:32.981
'cause you've literally been everything within that habitat.

2161
01:06:32.981 --> 01:06:33.997
Right?

2162
01:06:33.997 --> 01:06:37.579
And then versus like the men's circles that I'm holding,

2163
01:06:37.579 --> 01:06:38.576
you know,

2164
01:06:38.576 --> 01:06:39.409
in the U.K. it's like,

2165
01:06:39.409 --> 01:06:40.351
what,

2166
01:06:40.351 --> 01:06:42.032
the number one killer in men under the age of 50

2167
01:06:42.032 --> 01:06:42.865
is suicide.

2168
01:06:42.865 --> 01:06:43.698
Right?

2169
01:06:43.698 --> 01:06:46.481
So there's a... what's happening here?

2170
01:06:46.481 --> 01:06:47.314
Right?

2171
01:06:47.314 --> 01:06:48.238
Right

2172
01:06:48.238 --> 01:06:49.489
and there's something uniquely British about not...

2173
01:06:49.489 --> 01:06:50.322
you don't...

2174
01:06:50.322 --> 01:06:54.869
men are not demonstrative in their emotions here by default.

2175
01:06:54.869 --> 01:06:55.702
Right?

2176
01:06:55.702 --> 01:06:57.098
Well, again, I think-

2177
01:06:57.098 --> 01:06:58.677
There's a cultural norm around like-

2178
01:06:58.677 --> 01:07:00.410
Think of how far we go back, though.

2179
01:07:00.410 --> 01:07:01.243
It's like, where do we go?

2180
01:07:01.243 --> 01:07:03.930
'Cause if you think about the, say the Celt ancestors,

2181
01:07:03.930 --> 01:07:05.393
they were, again, about being

2182
01:07:05.393 --> 01:07:08.290
and being at one land and huge emotional stories

2183
01:07:08.290 --> 01:07:11.903
and weaving folks taught stories and song.

2184
01:07:11.903 --> 01:07:12.902
And is it...

2185
01:07:12.902 --> 01:07:14.879
it feels to me it's almost like

2186
01:07:14.879 --> 01:07:17.211
when the written word come in almost.

2187
01:07:17.211 --> 01:07:18.044
You know?

2188
01:07:18.044 --> 01:07:21.289
It's like that... what war did we lose in those processes?

2189
01:07:21.289 --> 01:07:24.453
But I think... 100% I think for the guys that I meet,

2190
01:07:24.453 --> 01:07:26.544
sudden you get them in a circle

2191
01:07:26.544 --> 01:07:29.184
and yet they're communicating all of a sudden.

2192
01:07:29.184 --> 01:07:31.009
You create a ceremony

2193
01:07:31.009 --> 01:07:32.583
and then it's as if

2194
01:07:32.583 --> 01:07:34.787
it's so in our DNA

2195
01:07:34.787 --> 01:07:36.695
to hold ceremony in circle.

2196
01:07:36.695 --> 01:07:40.538
When you create it, men open up and start sharing.

2197
01:07:40.538 --> 01:07:41.371
Mmm.

2198
01:07:41.371 --> 01:07:43.443
That is very different. You know?

2199
01:07:43.443 --> 01:07:45.070
So I think it's within us,

2200
01:07:45.070 --> 01:07:45.918
it's almost in those,

2201
01:07:45.918 --> 01:07:48.262
what I call the like the primordial union

2202
01:07:48.262 --> 01:07:50.525
or primordial databases within us.

2203
01:07:50.525 --> 01:07:51.358
Right?

2204
01:07:51.358 --> 01:07:52.792
There's something within our DNA

2205
01:07:52.792 --> 01:07:56.220
that ceremony and circle enables us to tap into that,

2206
01:07:56.220 --> 01:07:57.882
which is also again, a re-wilding, right?

2207
01:07:57.882 --> 01:07:58.715
Mm-hmm.

2208
01:07:58.715 --> 01:07:59.610
There's also letting stuff out.

2209
01:07:59.610 --> 01:08:03.007
I have guys like allowing them to roar and shout

2210
01:08:03.007 --> 01:08:04.618
and yell and express

2211
01:08:04.618 --> 01:08:07.257
that suddenly they put a lid on that

2212
01:08:07.257 --> 01:08:09.570
because they felt it was so inappropriate.

2213
01:08:09.570 --> 01:08:12.715
That level of masculinity, letting that stuff out.

2214
01:08:12.715 --> 01:08:13.548
Mm-hmm.

2215
01:08:13.548 --> 01:08:14.381
And why do we need to let that out?

2216
01:08:14.381 --> 01:08:15.654
Well, it's so it doesn't erupt in places

2217
01:08:15.654 --> 01:08:16.549
where it is inappropriate.

2218
01:08:16.549 --> 01:08:17.382
Right?

2219
01:08:17.382 --> 01:08:19.444
So it's giving them a modality like, "work on this."

2220
01:08:19.444 --> 01:08:21.017
Right. A healthy catharsis.

2221
01:08:21.017 --> 01:08:22.578
Yeah! And one of the guys,

2222
01:08:22.578 --> 01:08:23.476
he went into...

2223
01:08:23.476 --> 01:08:26.375
he said he hadn't been able to go to his local shops,

2224
01:08:26.375 --> 01:08:28.153
just couldn't get out to do it,

2225
01:08:28.153 --> 01:08:32.746
just felt disconnected and a level of depression, of course.

2226
01:08:32.746 --> 01:08:35.867
And then post-weekend, like 24 hours.

2227
01:08:35.867 --> 01:08:37.008
24 hour experience, right?

2228
01:08:37.008 --> 01:08:39.257
Went into his local town,

2229
01:08:39.257 --> 01:08:40.916
went into one of his local shops

2230
01:08:40.916 --> 01:08:42.624
and they were, "ah, how are you, man?"

2231
01:08:42.624 --> 01:08:43.701
He's like, "I'm great."

2232
01:08:43.701 --> 01:08:45.631
"Well we haven't seen you in ages.

2233
01:08:45.631 --> 01:08:46.464
(Rich and Tony chuckle)

2234
01:08:46.464 --> 01:08:47.297
Have you been on holiday?"

2235
01:08:47.297 --> 01:08:48.471
He's like, "no."

2236
01:08:48.471 --> 01:08:49.307
They said, "have you lost weight?

2237
01:08:49.307 --> 01:08:50.530
There's something very different about you.

2238
01:08:50.530 --> 01:08:53.567
You look... you look really... you look great!

2239
01:08:53.567 --> 01:08:54.400
And he said,

2240
01:08:54.400 --> 01:08:56.801
"yeah, I just went and spent 24 hours with this guy."

2241
01:08:56.801 --> 01:08:57.634
(Rich laughs)

2242
01:08:57.634 --> 01:08:58.467
You know?

2243
01:08:58.467 --> 01:08:59.300
Right.

2244
01:08:59.300 --> 01:09:01.062
Mixed play and unpacked it with them

2245
01:09:01.062 --> 01:09:03.653
and it's just, again, it was a playing with experience.

2246
01:09:03.653 --> 01:09:05.943
I had them in deep play for work,

2247
01:09:05.943 --> 01:09:09.254
like playing partner-partner work, forehead to forehead.

2248
01:09:09.254 --> 01:09:11.238
When one moves, the other one has to mirror the movement.

2249
01:09:11.238 --> 01:09:13.517
And I had them even sparring and play fighting

2250
01:09:13.517 --> 01:09:15.764
and rolling around and playing with each other's weights.

2251
01:09:15.764 --> 01:09:18.874
And again, things that we almost have lost

2252
01:09:18.874 --> 01:09:21.493
like that level of expression or human contact.

2253
01:09:21.493 --> 01:09:24.225
And I think partly like the three years we've had

2254
01:09:24.225 --> 01:09:26.660
has meant a real disconnect from human contact.

2255
01:09:26.660 --> 01:09:27.900
And I explained to one of the guys, like,

2256
01:09:27.900 --> 01:09:28.940
"think about it like this."

2257
01:09:28.940 --> 01:09:30.152
You wake up in the morning,

2258
01:09:30.152 --> 01:09:32.261
get hit with early light immediately, right?

2259
01:09:32.261 --> 01:09:34.355
Serotonin: one happy hormone. Tick!

2260
01:09:34.355 --> 01:09:36.728
Okay, he has a family. Okay, hugging.

2261
01:09:36.728 --> 01:09:37.866
Go and hug your family.

2262
01:09:37.866 --> 01:09:40.279
Oxytocin, another happy hormone, done!

2263
01:09:40.279 --> 01:09:41.841
All right, now get out and move more.

2264
01:09:41.841 --> 01:09:44.724
Okay, so then we have dopamine-seeking hormones

2265
01:09:44.724 --> 01:09:45.629
associated with happiness. Done!

2266
01:09:45.629 --> 01:09:47.330
Right now we have...

2267
01:09:47.330 --> 01:09:50.083
let's maybe up the intensity of it

2268
01:09:50.083 --> 01:09:51.731
and then we can bring endorphins in.

2269
01:09:51.731 --> 01:09:52.749
And now, all of a sudden, right,

2270
01:09:52.749 --> 01:09:53.812
we've got four happy hormones

2271
01:09:53.812 --> 01:09:55.103
you can put in the happy hormone shaker.

2272
01:09:55.103 --> 01:09:57.681
Give it a good shake and, bam, out you come!

2273
01:09:57.681 --> 01:09:59.005
And you could see

2274
01:09:59.005 --> 01:10:00.076
there was almost like,

2275
01:10:00.076 --> 01:10:00.909
the guy's like,

2276
01:10:00.909 --> 01:10:02.104
"yeah, but that sounds so simple!"

2277
01:10:02.104 --> 01:10:02.937
(Tony chuckles)

2278
01:10:02.937 --> 01:10:03.770
But it is!

2279
01:10:03.770 --> 01:10:05.519
Take me behind the velvet rope, Tony.

2280
01:10:05.519 --> 01:10:06.352
You know?

2281
01:10:06.352 --> 01:10:07.185
Come on.

2282
01:10:07.185 --> 01:10:08.018
It's so-

2283
01:10:08.018 --> 01:10:08.851
It's that thing,

2284
01:10:08.851 --> 01:10:11.510
there's an adage in recovery that's similar.

2285
01:10:11.510 --> 01:10:14.693
Like when you've been sober for a while and you, you know,

2286
01:10:14.693 --> 01:10:17.081
you're in this 12-step community,

2287
01:10:17.081 --> 01:10:19.941
at some point you reach this rubicon where you're like,

2288
01:10:19.941 --> 01:10:22.444
"yeah, I get it, man, but like, what's the next thing?

2289
01:10:22.444 --> 01:10:25.583
Like, what's the next... I've done all that stuff,

2290
01:10:25.583 --> 01:10:27.511
but I'm still struggling with this.

2291
01:10:27.511 --> 01:10:29.659
Tell me the secret that you haven't told me yet."

2292
01:10:29.659 --> 01:10:32.825
It's like, "no, it's just back to these principles."

2293
01:10:32.825 --> 01:10:33.658
Mmm.

2294
01:10:33.658 --> 01:10:34.491
You just need to practice them

2295
01:10:34.491 --> 01:10:35.693
a little bit more.

2296
01:10:35.693 --> 01:10:38.355
Like, the human mind wants to find...

2297
01:10:38.355 --> 01:10:40.728
and you see it like played out on social media,

2298
01:10:40.728 --> 01:10:42.650
Like what's the one thing that,

2299
01:10:42.650 --> 01:10:43.483
you know,

2300
01:10:43.483 --> 01:10:44.450
nobody's telling you?

2301
01:10:44.450 --> 01:10:46.562
And the truth is,

2302
01:10:46.562 --> 01:10:48.971
everything that you are

2303
01:10:48.971 --> 01:10:49.804
is about this.

2304
01:10:49.804 --> 01:10:52.402
Like, it is... there is no secret.

2305
01:10:52.402 --> 01:10:54.841
It's these very basic things

2306
01:10:54.841 --> 01:10:56.374
that we've always known

2307
01:10:56.374 --> 01:10:59.146
that we need to find a way to return to.

2308
01:10:59.146 --> 01:11:01.297
And the process of returning to them

2309
01:11:01.297 --> 01:11:04.455
involves unlearning so much of what, you know,

2310
01:11:04.455 --> 01:11:06.867
we've been indoctrinated in

2311
01:11:06.867 --> 01:11:10.932
and opening ourselves up in a childlike way-

2312
01:11:10.932 --> 01:11:11.765
Hmmm.

2313
01:11:11.765 --> 01:11:14.099
...to these, you know, innate pulls

2314
01:11:14.099 --> 01:11:15.384
that we all have

2315
01:11:15.384 --> 01:11:16.956
that connect us as humans.

2316
01:11:16.956 --> 01:11:18.465
Whether it's the campfire

2317
01:11:18.465 --> 01:11:19.566
or the breath exercise

2318
01:11:19.566 --> 01:11:22.427
or hugging your family members or like, you know,

2319
01:11:22.427 --> 01:11:26.077
embracing the day by, you know, acknowledging the sunlight

2320
01:11:26.077 --> 01:11:27.869
into your eyes upon awakening.

2321
01:11:27.869 --> 01:11:31.417
Like, all of these things are so crucial and fundamental,

2322
01:11:31.417 --> 01:11:34.859
and yet in this age of reason and enlightenment,

2323
01:11:34.859 --> 01:11:37.026
we dismiss them as trivial

2324
01:11:38.001 --> 01:11:39.532
because we exist

2325
01:11:39.532 --> 01:11:41.848
and value our identity

2326
01:11:41.848 --> 01:11:44.249
from a perspective of, you know,

2327
01:11:44.249 --> 01:11:46.368
what is going on in between our ears-

2328
01:11:46.368 --> 01:11:47.201
Mmm.

2329
01:11:47.201 --> 01:11:48.518
... the intellectualization of everything.

2330
01:11:48.518 --> 01:11:50.622
And this is like a thing I have with Julie.

2331
01:11:50.622 --> 01:11:52.106
She's, you know, more...

2332
01:11:52.106 --> 01:11:52.995
you know...

2333
01:11:52.995 --> 01:11:55.094
on the polarity of human experiences,

2334
01:11:55.094 --> 01:11:58.066
I would place her, you know, much closer to you.

2335
01:11:58.066 --> 01:11:59.492
And because of my upbringing,

2336
01:11:59.492 --> 01:12:00.595
my default setting

2337
01:12:00.595 --> 01:12:04.976
is to pivot back to that intellectualization of everything.

2338
01:12:04.976 --> 01:12:07.884
And I've grown a lot and become much more open

2339
01:12:07.884 --> 01:12:09.672
to different experiences

2340
01:12:09.672 --> 01:12:12.635
or we wouldn't even be having this conversation.

2341
01:12:12.635 --> 01:12:15.596
But, when stressed, I will revert, you know?

2342
01:12:15.596 --> 01:12:17.354
And then she's like, "what do you-"

2343
01:12:17.354 --> 01:12:18.187
(Rich laughs)

2344
01:12:18.187 --> 01:12:20.369
And it's hard. It's hard, man.

2345
01:12:20.369 --> 01:12:22.223
You know, it's like those...

2346
01:12:22.223 --> 01:12:23.741
because I can see,

2347
01:12:23.741 --> 01:12:26.690
you know, there's wisdom in both of these things.

2348
01:12:26.690 --> 01:12:28.379
They have to coexist on some level, right?

2349
01:12:28.379 --> 01:12:29.212
100%. Yeah, man.

2350
01:12:29.212 --> 01:12:30.823
And finding that right balance for me

2351
01:12:30.823 --> 01:12:34.409
of being open to what I know and to new experiences

2352
01:12:34.409 --> 01:12:35.781
and also, you know,

2353
01:12:35.781 --> 01:12:38.786
relying on the intellect when appropriate,

2354
01:12:38.786 --> 01:12:40.892
is like this dance that I'm...

2355
01:12:40.892 --> 01:12:41.821
I'm always in this...

2356
01:12:41.821 --> 01:12:45.236
it's not a war, it's more like a relationship.

2357
01:12:45.236 --> 01:12:46.069
Yeah.

2358
01:12:46.069 --> 01:12:47.940
Well there's symbiosis in that, right?

2359
01:12:47.940 --> 01:12:48.773
Mm-hmm.

2360
01:12:48.773 --> 01:12:49.606
Isn't there?

2361
01:12:49.606 --> 01:12:50.439
Sure.

2362
01:12:50.439 --> 01:12:51.272
I think,

2363
01:12:51.272 --> 01:12:52.105
you know,

2364
01:12:52.105 --> 01:12:53.361
as I said at the beginning of the conversation,

2365
01:12:53.361 --> 01:12:57.299
there is this information-rich and experienced pull moment

2366
01:12:57.299 --> 01:12:59.404
and it's just being mindful.

2367
01:12:59.404 --> 01:13:03.429
Like, is there values or is there a philosophy in there

2368
01:13:03.429 --> 01:13:04.973
somewhere within us, right?

2369
01:13:04.973 --> 01:13:06.148
That we can go...

2370
01:13:06.148 --> 01:13:07.728
well the information at least I'm gathering,

2371
01:13:07.728 --> 01:13:08.561
is just...

2372
01:13:08.561 --> 01:13:10.230
like for me, I have this physical, social,

2373
01:13:10.230 --> 01:13:11.063
spiritual understanding,

2374
01:13:11.063 --> 01:13:11.896
Right?

2375
01:13:11.896 --> 01:13:13.683
Within physical self, I know there's movement and play

2376
01:13:13.683 --> 01:13:15.959
and sleep and rest and how I eat and digest

2377
01:13:15.959 --> 01:13:17.876
and sunlight and water, right?

2378
01:13:17.876 --> 01:13:18.709
And sex, right?

2379
01:13:18.709 --> 01:13:19.542
Okay.

2380
01:13:19.542 --> 01:13:20.984
So the information I'm going to gather,

2381
01:13:20.984 --> 01:13:21.817
I'm gonna go and put this,

2382
01:13:21.817 --> 01:13:23.375
but what I'm gonna do now that I have all the information,

2383
01:13:23.375 --> 01:13:24.684
I'm going to implement it

2384
01:13:24.684 --> 01:13:25.517
and action it

2385
01:13:25.517 --> 01:13:26.784
and experience it

2386
01:13:26.784 --> 01:13:31.287
rather than get lost in this information the whole time.

2387
01:13:31.287 --> 01:13:32.120
It's a bit like studying, right?

2388
01:13:32.120 --> 01:13:32.953
Sure.

2389
01:13:32.953 --> 01:13:34.873
You can go from school to college,

2390
01:13:34.873 --> 01:13:37.226
university, and then post-grad stuff

2391
01:13:37.226 --> 01:13:38.059
and then keep going,

2392
01:13:38.059 --> 01:13:38.892
keep going,

2393
01:13:38.892 --> 01:13:39.725
keep going.

2394
01:13:39.725 --> 01:13:41.027
'Cause actually the big wide world

2395
01:13:41.027 --> 01:13:42.248
of when you finally you have to go and implement that stuff

2396
01:13:42.248 --> 01:13:43.081
can be quite scary.

2397
01:13:43.081 --> 01:13:46.093
So sometimes it's easier to remain in education

2398
01:13:46.093 --> 01:13:48.294
and also it sometimes helps feed the ego of

2399
01:13:48.294 --> 01:13:50.879
"when I do get involved in a conversation,

2400
01:13:50.879 --> 01:13:53.087
I can articulate that conversation well

2401
01:13:53.087 --> 01:13:54.631
and I have enough information behind me

2402
01:13:54.631 --> 01:13:55.767
to prove that I'm an intellect."

2403
01:13:55.767 --> 01:13:56.600
Right?

2404
01:13:56.600 --> 01:13:57.433
So there's...

2405
01:13:57.433 --> 01:13:58.903
or there might be a frustrated academic underneath it,

2406
01:13:58.903 --> 01:13:59.736
right?

2407
01:13:59.736 --> 01:14:00.637
That needs to learn.

2408
01:14:00.637 --> 01:14:02.248
And I very much went into information,

2409
01:14:02.248 --> 01:14:03.081
information,

2410
01:14:03.081 --> 01:14:03.914
information.

2411
01:14:03.914 --> 01:14:05.264
And then I go, right, okay,

2412
01:14:05.264 --> 01:14:07.484
experience, experience, experience, experience.

2413
01:14:07.484 --> 01:14:08.880
And I think that's a healthy balance.

2414
01:14:08.880 --> 01:14:10.247
It's like go and actually practice it.

2415
01:14:10.247 --> 01:14:13.661
Give it time, you know, give it the Yehudi time, right?

2416
01:14:13.661 --> 01:14:16.252
Know that this stuff's always gonna be here.

2417
01:14:16.252 --> 01:14:17.085
Mm-hmm.

2418
01:14:17.085 --> 01:14:19.712
We are so abundant of information,

2419
01:14:19.712 --> 01:14:22.258
but if we don't go and experience it... you know?

2420
01:14:22.258 --> 01:14:23.091
Right.

2421
01:14:23.091 --> 01:14:25.470
And, well, wisdom is birthed out of-

2422
01:14:25.470 --> 01:14:26.303
Yes.

2423
01:14:26.303 --> 01:14:28.809
...the experience of that information, right?

2424
01:14:28.809 --> 01:14:29.642
Yeah.

2425
01:14:29.642 --> 01:14:31.967
Like putting that information into action

2426
01:14:31.967 --> 01:14:34.421
from that, you know, is what arises with like,

2427
01:14:34.421 --> 01:14:36.737
we have too much information right now.

2428
01:14:36.737 --> 01:14:37.612
Not enough wisdom.

2429
01:14:37.612 --> 01:14:38.978
If you want the wisdom,

2430
01:14:38.978 --> 01:14:43.331
you've gotta apply the information and experience it.

2431
01:14:43.331 --> 01:14:44.164
Yeah.

2432
01:14:44.164 --> 01:14:46.835
'Cause, again, it's actioning is the growth, right?

2433
01:14:46.835 --> 01:14:49.670
So it's... growth happens in action, right?

2434
01:14:49.670 --> 01:14:51.519
Let's go and really experience this stuff.

2435
01:14:51.519 --> 01:14:56.260
And in that, you also find perhaps what it is for Rich,

2436
01:14:56.260 --> 01:14:58.229
what it is for Tony to experience it,

2437
01:14:58.229 --> 01:14:59.062
right?

2438
01:14:59.062 --> 01:15:01.173
So we get our own unique interpretation.

2439
01:15:01.173 --> 01:15:02.859
So it's not just our own unique interpretation,

2440
01:15:02.859 --> 01:15:05.629
it's also our unique way of it processing

2441
01:15:05.629 --> 01:15:08.018
and then perhaps expressing, right?

2442
01:15:08.018 --> 01:15:08.980
Mm-hmm.

2443
01:15:08.980 --> 01:15:10.647
So what has the universe uniquely assigned for you

2444
01:15:10.647 --> 01:15:11.585
and uniquely assigned for me?

2445
01:15:11.585 --> 01:15:12.704
It's completely different.

2446
01:15:12.704 --> 01:15:15.751
And the more and more I get to experience and be,

2447
01:15:15.751 --> 01:15:19.085
the more I get to fully tune into what that is.

2448
01:15:19.085 --> 01:15:19.918
Right?

2449
01:15:19.918 --> 01:15:20.751
Mm-hmm.

2450
01:15:20.751 --> 01:15:22.545
And to fully express what it is through me,

2451
01:15:22.545 --> 01:15:23.378
you know?

2452
01:15:23.378 --> 01:15:24.211
Mm-hmm.

2453
01:15:24.211 --> 01:15:25.930
Rather than maybe through the voice of another,

2454
01:15:25.930 --> 01:15:26.763
you know?

2455
01:15:26.763 --> 01:15:27.718
Right.

2456
01:15:27.718 --> 01:15:29.115
Yeah and I think in that place

2457
01:15:29.115 --> 01:15:31.644
you can find a deeper reservoir

2458
01:15:31.644 --> 01:15:34.709
of empathy and non-judgment of others.

2459
01:15:34.709 --> 01:15:35.596
Yeah.

2460
01:15:35.596 --> 01:15:37.806
There's a funny one around judgment

2461
01:15:37.806 --> 01:15:39.459
'cause I've, you know, in this,

2462
01:15:39.459 --> 01:15:41.174
in my kind of online community,

2463
01:15:41.174 --> 01:15:42.455
a few of them in there

2464
01:15:42.455 --> 01:15:45.214
are thinking what others think of them,

2465
01:15:45.214 --> 01:15:46.904
this judgment, you know?

2466
01:15:46.904 --> 01:15:48.820
It could be about the playful work

2467
01:15:48.820 --> 01:15:50.670
or hanging even on the tube,

2468
01:15:50.670 --> 01:15:53.792
or it could be anything within their environment, right?

2469
01:15:53.792 --> 01:15:55.348
And then it's, you know,

2470
01:15:55.348 --> 01:15:57.649
"I feel that people may be judging me."

2471
01:15:57.649 --> 01:15:59.616
And then you realize that, well it's judgment.

2472
01:15:59.616 --> 01:16:01.710
You are judging them for judging you.

2473
01:16:01.710 --> 01:16:02.543
Hmmm.

2474
01:16:02.543 --> 01:16:03.956
So judgment is the tier, right?

2475
01:16:03.956 --> 01:16:05.439
That's where we need to do the work, right?

2476
01:16:05.439 --> 01:16:06.272
(Tony and Rich laugh)

2477
01:16:06.272 --> 01:16:07.105
You know?

2478
01:16:07.105 --> 01:16:08.003
Yeah.

2479
01:16:08.003 --> 01:16:09.238
The meta-judgment.

2480
01:16:09.238 --> 01:16:10.579
Yeah! You know?

2481
01:16:10.579 --> 01:16:11.412
That's going on.

2482
01:16:11.412 --> 01:16:13.334
The bigger picture of judgment- what is that?

2483
01:16:13.334 --> 01:16:15.019
How dare you judge me judging you

2484
01:16:15.019 --> 01:16:16.640
judging me judging you?

2485
01:16:16.640 --> 01:16:17.473
Judging you.

2486
01:16:17.473 --> 01:16:18.306
Right.

2487
01:16:18.306 --> 01:16:19.951
Yeah. You know, that's there all right.

2488
01:16:19.951 --> 01:16:20.784
So,

2489
01:16:20.784 --> 01:16:23.894
the book is organized under these four principles,

2490
01:16:23.894 --> 01:16:27.201
all Rs, you know: reboot, reconnect, re-wild,

2491
01:16:27.201 --> 01:16:28.464
and then refine.

2492
01:16:28.464 --> 01:16:31.074
We've talked a little bit about unlearning-

2493
01:16:31.074 --> 01:16:31.907
Mmm.

2494
01:16:31.907 --> 01:16:33.806
...talked a little bit about reconnecting,

2495
01:16:33.806 --> 01:16:34.639
re-wilding.

2496
01:16:34.639 --> 01:16:37.092
What else can be said about this, you know,

2497
01:16:37.092 --> 01:16:40.342
process of understanding these pillars?

2498
01:16:42.032 --> 01:16:43.543
Well I think I look at rebooting,

2499
01:16:43.543 --> 01:16:44.671
it's almost like this...

2500
01:16:44.671 --> 01:16:47.444
there's a lot of practice in there for rebooting, right?

2501
01:16:47.444 --> 01:16:49.979
Even that, the breath that we've discussed

2502
01:16:49.979 --> 01:16:52.993
is an opportunity to just have a reboot in a moment.

2503
01:16:52.993 --> 01:16:53.826
You know?

2504
01:16:53.826 --> 01:16:55.573
Right, like big reboots.

2505
01:16:55.573 --> 01:16:56.550
Like full life reboots.

2506
01:16:56.550 --> 01:16:57.554
Like macro and micro.

2507
01:16:57.554 --> 01:16:58.859
All the way down to mini, yeah.

2508
01:16:58.859 --> 01:16:59.968
So it can... like, for me,

2509
01:16:59.968 --> 01:17:02.185
it's a very interesting period.

2510
01:17:02.185 --> 01:17:04.789
'Cause a lot of my stuff went online

2511
01:17:04.789 --> 01:17:05.715
and so I...

2512
01:17:05.715 --> 01:17:08.734
there's been an adjustment within that

2513
01:17:08.734 --> 01:17:11.643
that had to happen within our environment.

2514
01:17:11.643 --> 01:17:13.923
So when I have a studio that's set up,

2515
01:17:13.923 --> 01:17:15.626
and if I'm say, mentoring someone,

2516
01:17:15.626 --> 01:17:17.796
it's now more often than not,

2517
01:17:17.796 --> 01:17:22.068
it's online and sometimes you are receiving, you know,

2518
01:17:22.068 --> 01:17:23.996
all kinds of information, right?

2519
01:17:23.996 --> 01:17:27.386
And some of it's like, it's a lot in there to process.

2520
01:17:27.386 --> 01:17:29.578
And if I left that student, just opened up the door,

2521
01:17:29.578 --> 01:17:31.185
and walked into the house,

2522
01:17:31.185 --> 01:17:33.409
my family are them receiving that as well.

2523
01:17:33.409 --> 01:17:34.333
So for me it's, you know,

2524
01:17:34.333 --> 01:17:35.706
there's a reboot there.

2525
01:17:35.706 --> 01:17:37.718
"Okay, I'll just stop at the door,

2526
01:17:37.718 --> 01:17:39.968
take a breath, long exhale,

2527
01:17:40.989 --> 01:17:41.822
okay,

2528
01:17:41.822 --> 01:17:42.655
walk out."

2529
01:17:42.655 --> 01:17:44.087
And then the next door I open,

2530
01:17:44.087 --> 01:17:44.920
take a breath,

2531
01:17:44.920 --> 01:17:45.753
long exhale,

2532
01:17:45.753 --> 01:17:46.586
walk in.

2533
01:17:46.586 --> 01:17:47.991
You know, so just breathing.

2534
01:17:47.991 --> 01:17:50.190
Just imagine you had like a crazy day at the office

2535
01:17:50.190 --> 01:17:51.977
and then a crazy commute home

2536
01:17:51.977 --> 01:17:53.403
and you're carrying all that stuff

2537
01:17:53.403 --> 01:17:54.521
and then you arrive at the door

2538
01:17:54.521 --> 01:17:56.751
and you open up the door and you walk in with all that stuff

2539
01:17:56.751 --> 01:17:57.584
and you have kids-

2540
01:17:57.584 --> 01:17:59.418
Right. It all adds up-

2541
01:17:59.418 --> 01:18:01.121
...and the kid's dying to meet papa at that moment.

2542
01:18:01.121 --> 01:18:02.163
And it seems like a lifetime.

2543
01:18:02.163 --> 01:18:04.006
And then all of a sudden you've brought all this,

2544
01:18:04.006 --> 01:18:05.706
this kind of... you could call it toxic, right,

2545
01:18:05.706 --> 01:18:07.155
information in the house.

2546
01:18:07.155 --> 01:18:10.188
So that can be a reboot on a micro level, right?

2547
01:18:10.188 --> 01:18:11.404
A bigger reboot might be,

2548
01:18:11.404 --> 01:18:13.632
"okay, I'm gonna go and, you know,

2549
01:18:13.632 --> 01:18:15.728
I might get into an ice bath at home."

2550
01:18:15.728 --> 01:18:16.829
We have a couple of setups.

2551
01:18:16.829 --> 01:18:19.034
I have a barrel and have a big dip tank there.

2552
01:18:19.034 --> 01:18:22.275
And so that's, that's maybe on a bigger level of that.

2553
01:18:22.275 --> 01:18:24.514
Or you could go even higher than that

2554
01:18:24.514 --> 01:18:26.900
and I might go to psychedelics or something, you know,

2555
01:18:26.900 --> 01:18:28.642
to have a real kind of reboot.

2556
01:18:28.642 --> 01:18:30.422
Reconnecting that's, for me,

2557
01:18:30.422 --> 01:18:31.884
is mainly around reconnecting to

2558
01:18:31.884 --> 01:18:34.898
the fact that we are nature and not separate of it-

2559
01:18:34.898 --> 01:18:35.731
It's interconnected.

2560
01:18:35.731 --> 01:18:38.848
Us and nature, we are one in that sense.

2561
01:18:38.848 --> 01:18:41.823
So I think there's the spending more time

2562
01:18:41.823 --> 01:18:43.915
in those organic situations

2563
01:18:43.915 --> 01:18:46.471
to become more of an organic being

2564
01:18:46.471 --> 01:18:50.182
and to have more organic behaviors in those environments.

2565
01:18:50.182 --> 01:18:51.015
Everyday environments.

2566
01:18:51.015 --> 01:18:53.165
The more and more nature immersion,

2567
01:18:53.165 --> 01:18:55.675
the more natural the outcome will be, I would say.

2568
01:18:55.675 --> 01:18:57.775
And then trying to bring as much of that then

2569
01:18:57.775 --> 01:18:58.942
into your everyday environment.

2570
01:18:58.942 --> 01:19:00.701
So there's maybe that reconnection

2571
01:19:00.701 --> 01:19:01.736
starts off with yourself

2572
01:19:01.736 --> 01:19:03.436
and then perhaps then it moves out and

2573
01:19:03.436 --> 01:19:04.269
"oh, okay,

2574
01:19:04.269 --> 01:19:06.640
maybe I might want to be doing more around the environment

2575
01:19:06.640 --> 01:19:08.562
or environmental issues that are going on in the world.

2576
01:19:08.562 --> 01:19:09.491
But it starts, I think,

2577
01:19:09.491 --> 01:19:13.819
with the human within that conversation of biodiversity,

2578
01:19:13.819 --> 01:19:16.874
we have to reconnect to the fact that we are nature

2579
01:19:16.874 --> 01:19:18.298
and then we realize we're sitting around

2580
01:19:18.298 --> 01:19:20.104
this huge table of interdependence

2581
01:19:20.104 --> 01:19:22.204
with the plants, the rocks, and the animals

2582
01:19:22.204 --> 01:19:24.050
and it's all one thing, right?

2583
01:19:24.050 --> 01:19:26.279
And rather than seeing we're separate of it

2584
01:19:26.279 --> 01:19:27.582
or controlling of it.

2585
01:19:27.582 --> 01:19:29.224
Re-wilding is that state;

2586
01:19:29.224 --> 01:19:31.430
it's getting back to that position of,

2587
01:19:31.430 --> 01:19:32.289
well again,

2588
01:19:32.289 --> 01:19:34.825
what is it to move through a landscape,

2589
01:19:34.825 --> 01:19:35.951
to be the landscape,

2590
01:19:35.951 --> 01:19:37.566
to inhale the landscape.

2591
01:19:37.566 --> 01:19:40.523
Not just reconnecting to the fact we are it,

2592
01:19:40.523 --> 01:19:43.926
it's re-wilding all the behaviors within it, you know?

2593
01:19:43.926 --> 01:19:44.759
And then refinement is,

2594
01:19:44.759 --> 01:19:45.592
you know,

2595
01:19:45.592 --> 01:19:48.543
even when you think you've absolutely nailed it,

2596
01:19:48.543 --> 01:19:50.063
is to keep going back and keep going back

2597
01:19:50.063 --> 01:19:52.158
and keep going back to refine things.

2598
01:19:52.158 --> 01:19:52.991
Mm-hmm.

2599
01:19:52.991 --> 01:19:56.124
'Cause there's so much value in that refinement.

2600
01:19:56.124 --> 01:19:56.957
But more often than not,

2601
01:19:56.957 --> 01:19:59.142
I think along all of those journeys

2602
01:19:59.142 --> 01:20:00.917
is to go in with complete compassion

2603
01:20:00.917 --> 01:20:02.254
for yourself and others, right?

2604
01:20:02.254 --> 01:20:03.470
So there's a guy

2605
01:20:03.470 --> 01:20:07.107
on one of our last "100 Human Experiences."

2606
01:20:07.107 --> 01:20:11.365
He comes in and he delivers a practice on alignment.

2607
01:20:11.365 --> 01:20:13.844
So he had everyone sitting in a circle

2608
01:20:13.844 --> 01:20:15.510
on our bums, you know,

2609
01:20:15.510 --> 01:20:17.374
long sits, your legs are straight out in front of you,

2610
01:20:17.374 --> 01:20:18.622
but you're sitting upright,

2611
01:20:18.622 --> 01:20:19.455
all barefoot.

2612
01:20:19.455 --> 01:20:20.886
So there's like like a hundred people in a circle

2613
01:20:20.886 --> 01:20:22.035
with their feet altogether,

2614
01:20:22.035 --> 01:20:22.868
it looks amazing.

2615
01:20:22.868 --> 01:20:23.701
We got a fire pit in the middle.

2616
01:20:23.701 --> 01:20:24.534
Love that.

2617
01:20:24.534 --> 01:20:25.404
Just that alone-

2618
01:20:25.404 --> 01:20:26.237
(Rich laughs)

2619
01:20:26.237 --> 01:20:27.275
I was done at that point.

2620
01:20:27.275 --> 01:20:28.108
Yeah, like-

2621
01:20:28.108 --> 01:20:28.941
Don't need an alignment circle!

2622
01:20:28.941 --> 01:20:29.774
Yeah, there's no video,

2623
01:20:29.774 --> 01:20:30.607
but like,

2624
01:20:30.607 --> 01:20:32.795
Tony's lit up like a Christmas tree-

2625
01:20:32.795 --> 01:20:33.628
(Tony laughs)

2626
01:20:33.628 --> 01:20:34.461
...just imagining that

2627
01:20:34.461 --> 01:20:37.702
like this is your dharma and your heaven spot-

2628
01:20:37.702 --> 01:20:38.535
Oh, man.

2629
01:20:38.535 --> 01:20:39.545
...like a campfire

2630
01:20:39.545 --> 01:20:41.433
and a lot of bare feet pointed in your direction.

2631
01:20:41.433 --> 01:20:42.266
(Rich laughs)

2632
01:20:42.266 --> 01:20:43.871
Yeah and just doing deep work together, you know,

2633
01:20:43.871 --> 01:20:45.603
and going through that reboot, reconnect, re-wild.

2634
01:20:45.603 --> 01:20:46.436
Yeah.

2635
01:20:46.436 --> 01:20:47.269
This is the experience,

2636
01:20:47.269 --> 01:20:48.238
and he really brought something

2637
01:20:48.238 --> 01:20:50.877
that was quite special and it drove something within me.

2638
01:20:50.877 --> 01:20:51.715
So there's...

2639
01:20:51.715 --> 01:20:53.487
he would ask questions like,

2640
01:20:53.487 --> 01:20:55.495
it would be about alignment, it might be.

2641
01:20:55.495 --> 01:20:57.004
You know, we did a lot of voice-awakening work,

2642
01:20:57.004 --> 01:20:58.327
you know how I was saying at some stage

2643
01:20:58.327 --> 01:20:59.160
we've all been told like-

2644
01:20:59.160 --> 01:20:59.993
Mm-hmm.

2645
01:20:59.993 --> 01:21:01.244
...from the moment you're born, right?

2646
01:21:01.244 --> 01:21:02.660
You come out making all this noise in the world.

2647
01:21:02.660 --> 01:21:03.493
"Ahhh!"

2648
01:21:03.493 --> 01:21:05.837
And then everyone's like, "shh, shh, shh, shh, shh."

2649
01:21:05.837 --> 01:21:06.858
Don't speak unless spoken to.

2650
01:21:06.858 --> 01:21:07.691
Trying to keep you quiet!

2651
01:21:07.691 --> 01:21:09.850
Or the "children should be seen, not heard"

2652
01:21:09.850 --> 01:21:10.683
kind of behavior comes in

2653
01:21:10.683 --> 01:21:11.783
and then you sit in a classroom

2654
01:21:11.783 --> 01:21:13.630
where you have to put your hand up to even speak.

2655
01:21:13.630 --> 01:21:14.537
So the suppression of that-

2656
01:21:14.537 --> 01:21:16.306
And mistakes of what you're gonna say-

2657
01:21:16.306 --> 01:21:17.139
Yeah.

2658
01:21:17.139 --> 01:21:17.972
...are heightened.

2659
01:21:17.972 --> 01:21:19.397
So then we could say rebooting.

2660
01:21:19.397 --> 01:21:21.203
Rebooting would be a voice-awakening practice

2661
01:21:21.203 --> 01:21:23.422
to reconnect to the fact that I have this natural voice

2662
01:21:23.422 --> 01:21:24.933
and then we re-wild the voice, you know?

2663
01:21:24.933 --> 01:21:26.348
And then there's refinement within that,

2664
01:21:26.348 --> 01:21:29.017
even looking into that level.

2665
01:21:29.017 --> 01:21:30.843
So within that circle it's like,

2666
01:21:30.843 --> 01:21:32.134
well who...

2667
01:21:32.134 --> 01:21:33.810
we have a voice-awakening coach prior to that;

2668
01:21:33.810 --> 01:21:34.773
Her name's Kate Lister.

2669
01:21:34.773 --> 01:21:35.606
She is phenomenal.

2670
01:21:35.606 --> 01:21:37.557
So she gets everyone playing with their voice

2671
01:21:37.557 --> 01:21:39.460
and you get people that come up

2672
01:21:39.460 --> 01:21:41.334
and they're like a bit awkward, you know?

2673
01:21:41.334 --> 01:21:43.975
And, one guy, on the last... what was his name?

2674
01:21:43.975 --> 01:21:46.381
I won't mention his name, actually.

2675
01:21:46.381 --> 01:21:47.948
So he was a 55 year old dude

2676
01:21:47.948 --> 01:21:48.861
and he said,

2677
01:21:48.861 --> 01:21:51.304
"Oh Tony, when you asked me to come up speak

2678
01:21:51.304 --> 01:21:52.915
at the very beginning, I was so nervous."

2679
01:21:52.915 --> 01:21:55.735
And we actually unpacked it and went right back.

2680
01:21:55.735 --> 01:21:57.050
And it was school assembly-

2681
01:21:57.050 --> 01:21:57.883
Mmm.

2682
01:21:57.883 --> 01:21:59.414
...where the trauma came in.

2683
01:21:59.414 --> 01:22:00.587
So the school assembly was,

2684
01:22:00.587 --> 01:22:02.440
oh, he has to come out to the front stage

2685
01:22:02.440 --> 01:22:04.620
and talk to a whole tribe of people

2686
01:22:04.620 --> 01:22:05.453
that he probably hasn't,

2687
01:22:05.453 --> 01:22:06.286
you know,

2688
01:22:06.286 --> 01:22:08.572
he's only met a few of them that have become his mates.

2689
01:22:08.572 --> 01:22:11.021
And he now has to speak in front of that whole audience,

2690
01:22:11.021 --> 01:22:12.852
which some might excel at immediately,

2691
01:22:12.852 --> 01:22:15.215
but if you haven't been given the tools and the modalities

2692
01:22:15.215 --> 01:22:17.500
to be able to go up there, a bit like walking into the exam

2693
01:22:17.500 --> 01:22:18.333
doing breath before that,

2694
01:22:18.333 --> 01:22:19.813
then that's traumatic.

2695
01:22:19.813 --> 01:22:20.646
Mm-hmm.

2696
01:22:20.646 --> 01:22:22.418
It's not... so his PTSD was in there, right?

2697
01:22:22.418 --> 01:22:23.807
So whenever he has to stand up, he's like,

2698
01:22:23.807 --> 01:22:24.640
(Tony mimics stifled speech)

2699
01:22:24.640 --> 01:22:25.473
Right.

2700
01:22:25.473 --> 01:22:26.496
He can't speak.

2701
01:22:26.496 --> 01:22:28.850
So we gave him like voice-awakening work.

2702
01:22:28.850 --> 01:22:30.499
So then you sit in the circle and it would be,

2703
01:22:30.499 --> 01:22:31.332
Chris would say,

2704
01:22:31.332 --> 01:22:33.481
in this giant foot circle of 100 humans

2705
01:22:33.481 --> 01:22:34.525
in L-sits around a fire.

2706
01:22:34.525 --> 01:22:35.374
He would say,

2707
01:22:35.374 --> 01:22:38.228
"so if anyone of you came here today, you know,

2708
01:22:38.228 --> 01:22:40.016
maybe you had difficulty speaking your truth.

2709
01:22:40.016 --> 01:22:43.014
If you felt that you've now worked through that

2710
01:22:43.014 --> 01:22:44.510
and we've processed that,

2711
01:22:44.510 --> 01:22:46.162
do you think you can make a step forward?"

2712
01:22:46.162 --> 01:22:48.121
And they do like a... I called it the Angela Riddle,

2713
01:22:48.121 --> 01:22:48.954
which my mum,

2714
01:22:48.954 --> 01:22:50.494
she used to do these bum exercises,

2715
01:22:50.494 --> 01:22:51.379
in that L-sit position

2716
01:22:51.379 --> 01:22:53.138
and try and move around the lounge like that.

2717
01:22:53.138 --> 01:22:53.971
Mm-hmm.

2718
01:22:53.971 --> 01:22:56.288
So like hip hinging for a bum.

2719
01:22:56.288 --> 01:22:57.586
And so it was like this bum shuffle,

2720
01:22:57.586 --> 01:22:59.401
you'd make a bum shuffle forward

2721
01:22:59.401 --> 01:23:00.665
or you'd make a bum shuffle back

2722
01:23:00.665 --> 01:23:02.123
and he had these whole series of questions,

2723
01:23:02.123 --> 01:23:04.359
but you went through all the chakras this way, right?

2724
01:23:04.359 --> 01:23:05.239
It's fascinating, right?

2725
01:23:05.239 --> 01:23:08.629
And then eventually you had people forward,

2726
01:23:08.629 --> 01:23:09.462
people back,

2727
01:23:09.462 --> 01:23:10.626
all around this circle.

2728
01:23:10.626 --> 01:23:13.245
So they're no longer in this really organized circle,

2729
01:23:13.245 --> 01:23:14.875
it's very fragmented, right, in that sense.

2730
01:23:14.875 --> 01:23:16.391
But they're all moving towards the fire.

2731
01:23:16.391 --> 01:23:18.637
So they all have this purpose of getting to the fire,

2732
01:23:18.637 --> 01:23:19.520
this path.

2733
01:23:19.520 --> 01:23:22.278
And that was the thing about the path.

2734
01:23:22.278 --> 01:23:23.274
Look around you, look,

2735
01:23:23.274 --> 01:23:25.744
we're all walking towards the same direction,

2736
01:23:25.744 --> 01:23:28.146
but we're all at different stages, you know?

2737
01:23:28.146 --> 01:23:31.958
So we're all basically being asked of different things

2738
01:23:31.958 --> 01:23:33.121
and different processes

2739
01:23:33.121 --> 01:23:34.494
and we're all at different stages in life,

2740
01:23:34.494 --> 01:23:36.150
but ultimately we're all on the same path.

2741
01:23:36.150 --> 01:23:36.983
Mm-hmm.

2742
01:23:36.983 --> 01:23:38.188
And then he said,

2743
01:23:38.188 --> 01:23:39.358
"now just reach over.

2744
01:23:39.358 --> 01:23:41.073
Maybe that person in front of you

2745
01:23:41.073 --> 01:23:42.252
can just about reach them with your toe,

2746
01:23:42.252 --> 01:23:43.157
but reach and touch them.

2747
01:23:43.157 --> 01:23:44.676
The person behind you reach them with your fingers.

2748
01:23:44.676 --> 01:23:47.686
And now can you see that we're all connected?"

2749
01:23:47.686 --> 01:23:49.352
You know, on that path.

2750
01:23:49.352 --> 01:23:50.229
Yeah.

2751
01:23:50.229 --> 01:23:51.062
It was so powerful.

2752
01:23:51.062 --> 01:23:51.895
Beautiful.

2753
01:23:51.895 --> 01:23:52.728
You know?

2754
01:23:52.728 --> 01:23:53.561
Yeah.

2755
01:23:53.561 --> 01:23:57.072
Obviously all of this is very holistic

2756
01:23:57.072 --> 01:24:00.494
and on some level, individualistic.

2757
01:24:00.494 --> 01:24:04.367
These practices and modalities and lifestyle habits

2758
01:24:04.367 --> 01:24:06.126
are all about integrating

2759
01:24:06.126 --> 01:24:08.744
mind, body, spirit, et cetera.

2760
01:24:08.744 --> 01:24:11.561
The reductive human wants to say,

2761
01:24:11.561 --> 01:24:13.670
"Tony, just give me the three things,

2762
01:24:13.670 --> 01:24:14.811
like what do I,

2763
01:24:14.811 --> 01:24:15.665
you know,

2764
01:24:15.665 --> 01:24:17.115
what's the most important practice?

2765
01:24:17.115 --> 01:24:20.198
Or should I do breath or should I do meditation?

2766
01:24:20.198 --> 01:24:23.687
Or is it important that I do the cold immersion?"

2767
01:24:23.687 --> 01:24:25.344
Like that's the human animal.

2768
01:24:25.344 --> 01:24:26.177
Yeah, yeah.

2769
01:24:26.177 --> 01:24:27.010
Right?

2770
01:24:27.010 --> 01:24:28.869
This is a matrix of, you know,

2771
01:24:28.869 --> 01:24:30.351
countless practices,

2772
01:24:30.351 --> 01:24:31.877
some small, some big,

2773
01:24:31.877 --> 01:24:35.318
all of which you're free to experiment with.

2774
01:24:35.318 --> 01:24:36.151
Mmm.

2775
01:24:36.151 --> 01:24:36.984
All of which you can find,

2776
01:24:36.984 --> 01:24:37.817
you know,

2777
01:24:37.817 --> 01:24:38.650
in Tony's work

2778
01:24:38.650 --> 01:24:39.880
and in his book, et cetera.

2779
01:24:39.880 --> 01:24:41.989
And I'm sure you get this question a lot,

2780
01:24:41.989 --> 01:24:43.799
especially you're doing media around the book-

2781
01:24:43.799 --> 01:24:44.632
Yeah.

2782
01:24:44.632 --> 01:24:45.957
... like "what are the three things

2783
01:24:45.957 --> 01:24:46.790
that I should be doing

2784
01:24:46.790 --> 01:24:47.623
that I'm not doing?"

2785
01:24:47.623 --> 01:24:48.456
Or you know,

2786
01:24:48.456 --> 01:24:49.289
on some level,

2787
01:24:49.289 --> 01:24:50.679
it's about communicating these ideas

2788
01:24:50.679 --> 01:24:52.634
in a way that's digestible and practical

2789
01:24:52.634 --> 01:24:55.750
for somebody who's trying to understand

2790
01:24:55.750 --> 01:24:57.074
where you're coming from.

2791
01:24:57.074 --> 01:24:57.907
Well, again,

2792
01:24:57.907 --> 01:25:00.433
Nick Mulvey's lyrics always come to mind for me-

2793
01:25:00.433 --> 01:25:02.986
"Happy is the man who breathes in the morning."

2794
01:25:02.986 --> 01:25:04.470
It's not enough just to breathe in the morning.

2795
01:25:04.470 --> 01:25:05.503
So we need movement

2796
01:25:05.503 --> 01:25:08.797
and we need to kind of wake up that physicality, right?

2797
01:25:08.797 --> 01:25:10.451
And get into the vessel,

2798
01:25:10.451 --> 01:25:11.284
get grounded,

2799
01:25:11.284 --> 01:25:12.117
I would say.

2800
01:25:12.117 --> 01:25:12.950
So, move!

2801
01:25:12.950 --> 01:25:13.783
Move more.

2802
01:25:13.783 --> 01:25:14.616
You know?

2803
01:25:14.616 --> 01:25:15.941
And move in ways

2804
01:25:15.941 --> 01:25:20.238
that you can't really recognize as exercise in a sense.

2805
01:25:20.238 --> 01:25:22.990
That might mean sitting less on the couch,

2806
01:25:22.990 --> 01:25:23.823
you know?

2807
01:25:23.823 --> 01:25:26.209
Watching Netflix whilst being on the floor.

2808
01:25:26.209 --> 01:25:27.953
Play with different sitting positions.

2809
01:25:27.953 --> 01:25:28.972
If you're on Zoom,

2810
01:25:28.972 --> 01:25:30.881
maybe turn that hour long zoom session

2811
01:25:30.881 --> 01:25:32.980
into an hour mobility session.

2812
01:25:32.980 --> 01:25:35.173
You know, there's some ground sitting positions in the book,

2813
01:25:35.173 --> 01:25:36.006
right?

2814
01:25:36.006 --> 01:25:36.839
That you can play with.

2815
01:25:36.839 --> 01:25:37.672
There's six in there.

2816
01:25:37.672 --> 01:25:38.707
I have tutorials and things like that

2817
01:25:38.707 --> 01:25:41.470
you can have a look at, but have a little play.

2818
01:25:41.470 --> 01:25:42.303
And if you have kids,

2819
01:25:42.303 --> 01:25:43.944
just observe the kids on the ground,

2820
01:25:43.944 --> 01:25:44.777
how they move.

2821
01:25:44.777 --> 01:25:45.706
And they're your best teachers.

2822
01:25:45.706 --> 01:25:47.064
Like, "oh okay, I can do that,

2823
01:25:47.064 --> 01:25:47.897
I can do that,

2824
01:25:47.897 --> 01:25:48.730
I can't do that."

2825
01:25:48.730 --> 01:25:49.668
Just play with it,

2826
01:25:49.668 --> 01:25:50.521
and you'll find that

2827
01:25:50.521 --> 01:25:52.611
the more and more you play around on the ground,

2828
01:25:52.611 --> 01:25:54.217
the softer and more mobile you'll become over time.

2829
01:25:54.217 --> 01:25:55.979
So what might start off as stiff, you know,

2830
01:25:55.979 --> 01:25:57.896
you'll get signals to say, "that's enough now,

2831
01:25:57.896 --> 01:25:58.729
I need to move."

2832
01:25:58.729 --> 01:25:59.562
So, Rich,

2833
01:25:59.562 --> 01:26:00.395
I might be kneeling.

2834
01:26:00.395 --> 01:26:02.419
"It's a little bit of a needle there; it's a bit tender.

2835
01:26:02.419 --> 01:26:03.252
Okay, move.

2836
01:26:03.252 --> 01:26:04.085
Next thing, next movement."

2837
01:26:04.085 --> 01:26:05.480
And the more you move and the more...

2838
01:26:05.480 --> 01:26:06.620
then you go back to it.

2839
01:26:06.620 --> 01:26:09.943
So you stretch the discomfort over time

2840
01:26:09.943 --> 01:26:12.544
rather than sitting in discomfort for too long,

2841
01:26:12.544 --> 01:26:13.942
getting an emotional response

2842
01:26:13.942 --> 01:26:14.775
and then going,

2843
01:26:14.775 --> 01:26:15.785
"no, I can't hack this anymore.

2844
01:26:15.785 --> 01:26:16.783
It doesn't work,"

2845
01:26:16.783 --> 01:26:18.308
just play with the edges

2846
01:26:18.308 --> 01:26:19.951
of discomfort and comfort

2847
01:26:19.951 --> 01:26:21.650
until you can push the boundaries in that,

2848
01:26:21.650 --> 01:26:22.483
until eventually,

2849
01:26:22.483 --> 01:26:23.316
like me,

2850
01:26:23.316 --> 01:26:25.459
sitting becomes more uncomfortable for me

2851
01:26:25.459 --> 01:26:26.462
than actually being on the ground.

2852
01:26:26.462 --> 01:26:28.090
I much prefer being on the ground

2853
01:26:28.090 --> 01:26:30.530
and it's assisted so much with my endurance work.

2854
01:26:30.530 --> 01:26:33.247
I think in the documentary there's a...

2855
01:26:33.247 --> 01:26:34.814
the "One Man Two Feet, Three Peaks.,"

2856
01:26:34.814 --> 01:26:38.186
I've just run up Snowdon and back down again

2857
01:26:38.186 --> 01:26:41.428
and then completed two marathons after that.

2858
01:26:41.428 --> 01:26:45.067
And there's a whole elevation of like 7,400 that day.

2859
01:26:45.067 --> 01:26:46.810
And we get back to a campsite

2860
01:26:46.810 --> 01:26:48.621
and I'm now kneeling on the ground

2861
01:26:48.621 --> 01:26:50.572
eating food with my kids, you know?

2862
01:26:50.572 --> 01:26:53.421
And that mobility stuff on the ground

2863
01:26:53.421 --> 01:26:56.328
enables me to then stand up and move again.

2864
01:26:56.328 --> 01:26:57.161
Mm-hmm.

2865
01:26:57.161 --> 01:26:58.894
If I went to sitting, I'd get so locked up

2866
01:26:58.894 --> 01:27:00.322
in hips and ankles and everything else.

2867
01:27:00.322 --> 01:27:01.155
So just try and, yeah,

2868
01:27:01.155 --> 01:27:02.542
think about nourishing movement

2869
01:27:02.542 --> 01:27:04.724
and the movement will enable other practices.

2870
01:27:04.724 --> 01:27:06.982
Breath: great, easy, simple breathing practices.

2871
01:27:06.982 --> 01:27:08.165
You know, it's free.

2872
01:27:08.165 --> 01:27:09.819
Movement is free on the ground.

2873
01:27:09.819 --> 01:27:11.068
Don't need a gym membership for that.

2874
01:27:11.068 --> 01:27:13.164
Don't need to exercise; working from home anyway.

2875
01:27:13.164 --> 01:27:14.981
Just improve that space.

2876
01:27:14.981 --> 01:27:17.846
Create a space where you can move to begin with I guess.

2877
01:27:17.846 --> 01:27:18.679
Right?

2878
01:27:18.679 --> 01:27:19.512
So that's that.

2879
01:27:19.512 --> 01:27:23.091
I would then look at, right, the voice work.

2880
01:27:23.091 --> 01:27:26.833
If you have trouble speaking or articulating,

2881
01:27:26.833 --> 01:27:27.963
breathing helps

2882
01:27:27.963 --> 01:27:30.364
because then you can remain calm

2883
01:27:30.364 --> 01:27:32.126
when that upregulated voice comes in.

2884
01:27:32.126 --> 01:27:33.276
You can breathe that.

2885
01:27:33.276 --> 01:27:34.738
But also opening this stuff up,

2886
01:27:34.738 --> 01:27:35.896
I'd get a cushion

2887
01:27:35.896 --> 01:27:39.249
and like scream and yell into the cushion

2888
01:27:39.249 --> 01:27:40.385
and let stuff out.

2889
01:27:40.385 --> 01:27:42.587
Just really have a practice of that.

2890
01:27:42.587 --> 01:27:44.582
It doesn't have to be with the voice coach

2891
01:27:44.582 --> 01:27:46.427
in a big 100 human circle

2892
01:27:46.427 --> 01:27:49.285
It can just be in your apartment with a pillow.

2893
01:27:49.285 --> 01:27:50.147
Mm-hmm.

2894
01:27:50.147 --> 01:27:51.694
If things get too much for you

2895
01:27:51.694 --> 01:27:53.391
and you feel like you have to let go,

2896
01:27:53.391 --> 01:27:55.870
it's much better to let go than screw the lid even tighter.

2897
01:27:55.870 --> 01:27:56.703
You know?

2898
01:27:56.703 --> 01:27:57.936
Be playful.

2899
01:27:57.936 --> 01:28:00.693
You know, can you just look at maybe

2900
01:28:00.693 --> 01:28:02.755
what's an adult version of the play stuff

2901
01:28:02.755 --> 01:28:04.119
that we can think of?

2902
01:28:04.119 --> 01:28:06.077
Dance, you know?

2903
01:28:06.077 --> 01:28:09.093
Put music on and play your physicality.

2904
