3222
01:37:52.750 --> 01:37:54.366
No, they spend 10 and a half hours sitting-

3223
01:37:54.366 --> 01:37:55.199
Right.

3224
01:37:55.199 --> 01:37:56.187
...just their 10 and a half hours

3225
01:37:56.187 --> 01:37:58.112
are on the ground sitting.

3226
01:37:58.112 --> 01:37:59.957
And every ground rest position is,

3227
01:37:59.957 --> 01:38:00.988
we could call,

3228
01:38:00.988 --> 01:38:01.864
like a prerequisite

3229
01:38:01.864 --> 01:38:03.932
for something that has to be involved,

3230
01:38:03.932 --> 01:38:05.520
engaged into how we stand,

3231
01:38:05.520 --> 01:38:07.892
then how we walk, and how we run.

3232
01:38:07.892 --> 01:38:11.218
So when we just go to one sitting form in a chair,

3233
01:38:11.218 --> 01:38:13.599
which isn't conducive with standing up,

3234
01:38:13.599 --> 01:38:16.982
there's little wonder why we have chronic back conditions,

3235
01:38:16.982 --> 01:38:18.739
neck conditions, even knee conditions.

3236
01:38:18.739 --> 01:38:20.714
'Cause we are no longer taking the knee, even,

3237
01:38:20.714 --> 01:38:22.807
into the depths of range that it needs.

3238
01:38:22.807 --> 01:38:23.640
Yeah?

3239
01:38:23.640 --> 01:38:24.473
Yeah.

3240
01:38:24.473 --> 01:38:25.998
So it's then not about the...

3241
01:38:25.998 --> 01:38:26.831
not about...

3242
01:38:26.831 --> 01:38:28.114
it's basically quick fixes

3243
01:38:28.114 --> 01:38:31.050
of further distractions from the truth.

3244
01:38:31.050 --> 01:38:32.828
And the truth is we just don't move enough, right?

3245
01:38:32.828 --> 01:38:35.305
And we sit for long periods of time,

3246
01:38:35.305 --> 01:38:37.476
but in inappropriate shapes,

3247
01:38:37.476 --> 01:38:39.133
which then create symptoms.

3248
01:38:39.133 --> 01:38:41.290
And then we are trying to then search a symptom relief.

3249
01:38:41.290 --> 01:38:42.340
So we go and see this specialist,

3250
01:38:42.340 --> 01:38:43.173
this specialist,

3251
01:38:43.173 --> 01:38:44.006
this specialist,

3252
01:38:44.006 --> 01:38:45.576
but we haven't changed the behavior.

3253
01:38:45.576 --> 01:38:46.409
Right.

3254
01:38:46.409 --> 01:38:48.916
You know, so I would go to the...

3255
01:38:48.916 --> 01:38:51.539
I deal with the cause level for me personally,

3256
01:38:51.539 --> 01:38:54.493
that's where I've always gone with back's and knee injuries,

3257
01:38:54.493 --> 01:38:57.855
it's to get the optimal or natural ranges back into them.

3258
01:38:57.855 --> 01:38:58.688
Right?

3259
01:38:58.688 --> 01:38:59.521
Right.

3260
01:38:59.521 --> 01:39:00.354
So that would begin-

3261
01:39:00.354 --> 01:39:01.250
And still-

3262
01:39:01.250 --> 01:39:02.083
Go ahead.

3263
01:39:02.083 --> 01:39:02.916
You still have...

3264
01:39:02.916 --> 01:39:03.749
'cause you're still having symptom relief

3265
01:39:03.749 --> 01:39:05.764
like you go and see this person, this person,

3266
01:39:05.764 --> 01:39:06.701
but then what are you doing with that?

3267
01:39:06.701 --> 01:39:07.579
Otherwise it's more information.

3268
01:39:07.579 --> 01:39:08.412
Right?

3269
01:39:08.412 --> 01:39:09.245
Yeah.

3270
01:39:09.245 --> 01:39:10.208
And what I need to do is then

3271
01:39:10.208 --> 01:39:11.832
flip the experience and say,

3272
01:39:11.832 --> 01:39:14.154
"well what's the natural sitting positions?

3273
01:39:14.154 --> 01:39:14.987
Right?

3274
01:39:14.987 --> 01:39:16.026
Let's just keep doing this stuff

3275
01:39:16.026 --> 01:39:18.025
'cause the symptom stuff's working for me right now.

3276
01:39:18.025 --> 01:39:19.982
It really helps to go and see this practitioner.

3277
01:39:19.982 --> 01:39:21.236
Sometimes that's just an emotional hug.

3278
01:39:21.236 --> 01:39:22.069
Right?

3279
01:39:22.069 --> 01:39:23.493
That's what that becomes.

3280
01:39:23.493 --> 01:39:24.566
Because it's chronic,

3281
01:39:24.566 --> 01:39:25.561
it's sometimes...

3282
01:39:25.561 --> 01:39:27.533
it's no longer existing where it did.

3283
01:39:27.533 --> 01:39:28.366
Right?

3284
01:39:28.366 --> 01:39:29.447
Sometimes there's even a blockade

3285
01:39:29.447 --> 01:39:31.048
and we hold onto it for a bit longer

3286
01:39:31.048 --> 01:39:32.743
and we have to find a way of mechanism releasing it

3287
01:39:32.743 --> 01:39:34.992
but then keep going back into this.

3288
01:39:34.992 --> 01:39:36.640
Like trigger point work is fantastic

3289
01:39:36.640 --> 01:39:38.108
but it's not fantastic on its own

3290
01:39:38.108 --> 01:39:39.014
'cause you have to go back

3291
01:39:39.014 --> 01:39:40.522
and see the trigger point specialist again.

3292
01:39:40.522 --> 01:39:41.744
Have a trigger point specialist

3293
01:39:41.744 --> 01:39:44.456
and then go and change up your movement

3294
01:39:44.456 --> 01:39:47.227
and make your movement as organic as possible.

3295
01:39:47.227 --> 01:39:50.028
So I would go try and flip, even to start with,

3296
01:39:50.028 --> 01:39:51.599
'casue it seems so extreme to think,

3297
01:39:51.599 --> 01:39:53.475
"oh, I'm gonna suddenly go and sit on the floor

3298
01:39:53.475 --> 01:39:54.308
for 10 and a half hours."

3299
01:39:54.308 --> 01:39:56.454
Just do segments of it.

3300
01:39:56.454 --> 01:39:57.287
Mm-hmm.

3301
01:39:57.287 --> 01:39:59.066
And bring more of it into your every day,

3302
01:39:59.066 --> 01:39:59.899
you know?

3303
01:39:59.899 --> 01:40:00.732
Yeah.

3304
01:40:00.732 --> 01:40:02.032
Otherwise it's seated posture

3305
01:40:02.032 --> 01:40:04.570
that affects the way that the hip joints behave,

3306
01:40:04.570 --> 01:40:06.123
affects the way the pelvis behaves

3307
01:40:06.123 --> 01:40:08.452
'cause you've created like counter-mutation with the pelvis,

3308
01:40:08.452 --> 01:40:10.305
compromises the S.I. joints.

3309
01:40:10.305 --> 01:40:12.084
Abs are off right now;

3310
01:40:12.084 --> 01:40:13.582
I have to work really hard

3311
01:40:13.582 --> 01:40:14.468
to remain upright.

3312
01:40:14.468 --> 01:40:17.075
Mid back and shoulders can pop up.

3313
01:40:17.075 --> 01:40:17.908
Right?

3314
01:40:17.908 --> 01:40:19.332
There's so much that happens just from sitting

3315
01:40:19.332 --> 01:40:21.493
and the more compliant the chair,

3316
01:40:21.493 --> 01:40:23.110
the more stiff we become in it

3317
01:40:23.110 --> 01:40:24.702
and the more awkward the positions we get into.

3318
01:40:24.702 --> 01:40:25.535
Right?

3319
01:40:25.535 --> 01:40:26.368
Right.

3320
01:40:26.368 --> 01:40:27.516
Whereas if you sit on a really hard seat,

3321
01:40:27.516 --> 01:40:29.170
suddenly you are actually more aware.

3322
01:40:29.170 --> 01:40:31.072
If you sit on a really hard floor, you'll be more aware.

3323
01:40:31.072 --> 01:40:32.216
Sit on a really cushioned floor.

3324
01:40:32.216 --> 01:40:33.049
You have...

3325
01:40:33.049 --> 01:40:34.785
it's a bit more sympathetic to play with,

3326
01:40:34.785 --> 01:40:36.038
so that's sometimes nicer.

3327
01:40:36.038 --> 01:40:38.834
Then you can use supports and bolsters and things to help.

3328
01:40:38.834 --> 01:40:40.434
So if you're sitting cross-legged,

3329
01:40:40.434 --> 01:40:41.909
maybe to start if it's too intense,

3330
01:40:41.909 --> 01:40:43.600
put bolster underneath your butt.

3331
01:40:43.600 --> 01:40:45.081
If you are sitting in a squat

3332
01:40:45.081 --> 01:40:46.324
and you can't get down there

3333
01:40:46.324 --> 01:40:47.569
'cause your ankles aren't quite flexible enough,

3334
01:40:47.569 --> 01:40:49.493
put a little wedge behind your heels

3335
01:40:49.493 --> 01:40:53.275
and allow your pelvis to relax in those sitting positions.

3336
01:40:53.275 --> 01:40:55.615
'Cause often there's tension there as well.

3337
01:40:55.615 --> 01:40:58.023
So like relaxing the pelvic floor really helps.

3338
01:40:58.023 --> 01:41:00.540
Think lower abdomen, let that stuff go.

3339
01:41:00.540 --> 01:41:02.402
And then look at the behaviors of the joints.

3340
01:41:02.402 --> 01:41:03.235
Right?

3341
01:41:03.235 --> 01:41:04.068
How do I mobilize the ankle more?

3342
01:41:04.068 --> 01:41:06.309
How can I mobilize my hip more?

3343
01:41:06.309 --> 01:41:07.714
And the more mobile the hip,

3344
01:41:07.714 --> 01:41:08.902
the more stable the knee.

3345
01:41:08.902 --> 01:41:09.735
The more stable the knee,

3346
01:41:09.735 --> 01:41:10.568
the more mobile the hip.

3347
01:41:10.568 --> 01:41:11.401
The more mobile the hip,

3348
01:41:11.401 --> 01:41:13.262
the more stable the pelvis and the lumbar.

3349
01:41:13.262 --> 01:41:14.095
And think about that,

3350
01:41:14.095 --> 01:41:15.885
even that joint-by-joint approach.

3351
01:41:15.885 --> 01:41:16.718
I mean

3352
01:41:16.718 --> 01:41:18.034
if you apply that joint-by-joint approach

3353
01:41:18.034 --> 01:41:19.969
to how we're sitting now... yeah.

3354
01:41:19.969 --> 01:41:20.802
Right.

3355
01:41:20.802 --> 01:41:22.272
Where's the ankle mobility?

3356
01:41:22.272 --> 01:41:24.375
Where's the hip mobility and where's the knee stability?

3357
01:41:24.375 --> 01:41:27.217
So unfortunately it has to be lumbar, pelvis,

3358
01:41:27.217 --> 01:41:28.080
and then the mid-back.

3359
01:41:28.080 --> 01:41:30.279
And we all know what the couching, slouching,

3360
01:41:30.279 --> 01:41:33.463
surfing, swiping type of posture looks like.

3361
01:41:33.463 --> 01:41:34.296
Mm-hmm.

3362
01:41:34.296 --> 01:41:36.755
It's really evident in that thoracic spine

3363
01:41:36.755 --> 01:41:39.111
gets a real kyphosis going.

3364
01:41:39.111 --> 01:41:39.944
Right?

3365
01:41:39.944 --> 01:41:41.418
And the head position ends up more forward.

3366
01:41:41.418 --> 01:41:42.793
And the problem with that then, again,

3367
01:41:42.793 --> 01:41:44.877
is that when you do go to walk,

3368
01:41:44.877 --> 01:41:46.158
we are no longer aligned.

3369
01:41:46.158 --> 01:41:47.120
The head isn't up,

3370
01:41:47.120 --> 01:41:47.953
the chest isn't up,

3371
01:41:47.953 --> 01:41:51.199
the pelvis and all those three aren't stacked appropriately.

3372
01:41:51.199 --> 01:41:52.770
The head's a huge weight.

3373
01:41:52.770 --> 01:41:54.609
The more forward it is of that base of support,

3374
01:41:54.609 --> 01:41:56.154
the longer you have to stride.

3375
01:41:56.154 --> 01:41:57.928
The longer your levers,

3376
01:41:57.928 --> 01:41:59.865
the more forces you have to deal.

3377
01:41:59.865 --> 01:42:00.728
You're tall, right?

3378
01:42:00.728 --> 01:42:02.623
So you have to do even more work, right?

3379
01:42:02.623 --> 01:42:04.636
Because of the length of your levers.

3380
01:42:04.636 --> 01:42:07.327
And I often discuss this with parents

3381
01:42:07.327 --> 01:42:08.160
with kids

3382
01:42:08.160 --> 01:42:11.994
and if you don't keep these modalities of movement alive

3383
01:42:11.994 --> 01:42:14.450
and you go into a school environment

3384
01:42:14.450 --> 01:42:16.466
and you don't keep the movement modalities alive

3385
01:42:16.466 --> 01:42:17.554
as a parent outside of that.

3386
01:42:17.554 --> 01:42:18.387
Right?

3387
01:42:18.387 --> 01:42:19.434
Like parkour's great for that

3388
01:42:19.434 --> 01:42:21.307
and free running is great for that

3389
01:42:21.307 --> 01:42:23.237
'cause they're really expressing their physicality

3390
01:42:23.237 --> 01:42:24.396
and it's very natural.

3391
01:42:24.396 --> 01:42:26.261
That when you get to a certain age,

3392
01:42:26.261 --> 01:42:27.094
teenage years,

3393
01:42:27.094 --> 01:42:30.772
you're suddenly having massive growth spurts.

3394
01:42:30.772 --> 01:42:33.786
And whereas if you were divorced from movement

3395
01:42:33.786 --> 01:42:36.501
and you suddenly weren't moving around how nature intended

3396
01:42:36.501 --> 01:42:38.027
and suddenly you have a growth spurt,

3397
01:42:38.027 --> 01:42:39.965
it's like baby giraffes walking around-

3398
01:42:39.965 --> 01:42:40.798
Right.

3399
01:42:40.798 --> 01:42:42.560
...with no idea how to move their limbs anymore.

3400
01:42:42.560 --> 01:42:44.196
Whereas if you carried on moving naturally

3401
01:42:44.196 --> 01:42:45.029
throughout your day,

3402
01:42:45.029 --> 01:42:47.108
like punctuated and amongst your day,

3403
01:42:47.108 --> 01:42:48.283
"I'm gonna just sit more on the ground

3404
01:42:48.283 --> 01:42:50.177
or I'm gonna hang or do this,"

3405
01:42:50.177 --> 01:42:53.701
suddenly those growth spurts aren't so alarming

3406
01:42:53.701 --> 01:42:56.427
because you've created a micro kind of adjustment

3407
01:42:56.427 --> 01:42:57.491
as you've addressed it.

3408
01:42:57.491 --> 01:42:58.324
Mmm.

3409
01:42:58.324 --> 01:43:00.526
So I'd really think about,

3410
01:43:00.526 --> 01:43:01.954
it's the everyday stuff.

3411
01:43:01.954 --> 01:43:03.123
It's the environment stuff.

3412
01:43:03.123 --> 01:43:04.991
What can you take control of in your everyday habitat?

3413
01:43:04.991 --> 01:43:06.251
In your everyday environment?

3414
01:43:06.251 --> 01:43:08.047
'Cause otherwise all of that work is just,

3415
01:43:08.047 --> 01:43:09.615
it's literally symptom relief

3416
01:43:09.615 --> 01:43:12.023
and you really need to get to the cause of it, you know?

3417
01:43:12.023 --> 01:43:12.856
Yeah.

3418
01:43:12.856 --> 01:43:13.689
Cause we might be going,

3419
01:43:13.689 --> 01:43:14.838
"oh, running's the cause" or

3420
01:43:14.838 --> 01:43:16.022
"cycling on the bike's the cause.

3421
01:43:16.022 --> 01:43:18.742
I would say it's the stuff that you've been doing

3422
01:43:18.742 --> 01:43:20.068
for 10 and a half hours a day

3423
01:43:20.068 --> 01:43:20.901
that isn't natural-

3424
01:43:20.901 --> 01:43:21.734
Right.

3425
01:43:21.734 --> 01:43:22.829
...that then you go and try and run with

3426
01:43:22.829 --> 01:43:23.688
and try and cycle with-

3427
01:43:23.688 --> 01:43:24.521
Yeah.

3428
01:43:24.521 --> 01:43:25.783
...that then compromises that chain.

3429
01:43:25.783 --> 01:43:26.616
Yeah.

3430
01:43:26.616 --> 01:43:27.984
I mean I think I shared this last time,

3431
01:43:27.984 --> 01:43:28.817
like,

3432
01:43:28.817 --> 01:43:31.484
my kind of default is, you know,

3433
01:43:32.647 --> 01:43:34.087
sitting doing like this.

3434
01:43:34.087 --> 01:43:34.920
Yeah.

3435
01:43:34.920 --> 01:43:37.621
Or at a desk preparing to do something like this

3436
01:43:37.621 --> 01:43:40.157
